#: src\protocol.md
msgid "The important distinction is **capability presence versus compatibility parity**. A parser or transport implementation existing in the codebase does not automatically mean every upstream option, version, flow mode, or client is supported."
msgstr "需要特别区分 **存在某项能力** 与 **达到完整兼容**。代码库中存在某个解析器或传输实现，并不自动意味着所有上游选项、版本、flow 模式或客户端都得到支持。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Choosing a Starting Point"
msgstr "选择阅读与使用起点"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Local application proxying"
msgstr "本地应用代理"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Start with [SOCKS5](./protocols/socks5.md) or [HTTP Proxy](./protocols/http.md). These are the easiest ways to validate the client core before adding TUN, transparent routing, or DNS interception."
msgstr "建议从 [SOCKS5](./protocols/socks5.md) 或 [HTTP 代理](./protocols/http.md) 开始。在加入 TUN、透明路由或 DNS 拦截之前，这是验证客户端核心最简单的方式。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Simple TLS-based remote proxy"
msgstr "简单的 TLS 远程代理"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Use [Trojan](./protocols/trojan.md) as the reference for the baseline TLS + password protocol model. If an implementation adds WebSocket or another transport, treat that as an additional layer."
msgstr "可将 [Trojan](./protocols/trojan.md) 作为基础 TLS + 密码认证协议模型的参考。如果某个实现额外加入 WebSocket 或其他传输方式，应将其视为附加层。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "UDP/QUIC-oriented remote proxying"
msgstr "面向 UDP/QUIC 的远程代理"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Compare [Hysteria 2](./protocols/hysteria2.md) and [TUIC](./protocols/tuic.md). Both rely heavily on a healthy UDP path, but their authentication, task model, and UDP-relay framing differ."
msgstr "可以对比 [Hysteria 2](./protocols/hysteria2.md) 与 [TUIC](./protocols/tuic.md)。二者都高度依赖健康的 UDP 路径，但认证方式、任务模型和 UDP 转发封装各不相同。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Xray-style layered deployments"
msgstr "Xray 风格的分层部署"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Read these together:"
msgstr "建议将以下页面结合阅读："

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[VLESS](./protocols/vless.md) — proxy protocol and user identity."
msgstr "[VLESS](./protocols/vless.md) — 代理协议与用户身份层。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[XHTTP](./protocols/xhttp.md) — optional HTTP-oriented transport."
msgstr "[XHTTP](./protocols/xhttp.md) — 可选的 HTTP 风格传输层。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[REALITY](./protocols/reality.md) — optional transport-security layer."
msgstr "[REALITY](./protocols/reality.md) — 可选的传输安全层。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Keeping the three layers separate makes configuration and troubleshooting much easier."
msgstr "明确区分这三个层级，可以显著降低配置和排障难度。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Security Rules of Thumb"
msgstr "安全经验原则"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "SOCKS5 and a local HTTP proxy do not provide encryption by themselves."
msgstr "SOCKS5 和本地 HTTP 代理本身不提供加密。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Do not expose unauthenticated local proxy listeners to the public internet."
msgstr "不要把未认证的本地代理监听器暴露到公网。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Keep certificate verification enabled for TLS-based remote protocols."
msgstr "对于基于 TLS 的远程协议，应保持证书验证开启。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Treat REALITY private keys, Trojan passwords, Hysteria credentials, and TUIC passwords as secrets."
msgstr "REALITY 私钥、Trojan 密码、Hysteria 凭据和 TUIC 密码都应作为敏感信息妥善保护。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "For QUIC-based protocols, verify UDP reachability before changing protocol tuning."
msgstr "对于基于 QUIC 的协议，在调整协议参数之前应先确认 UDP 可达性。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Validate the exact proxy + transport + security combination supported by the selected core rather than assuming configuration portability."
msgstr "应验证当前核心真正支持的代理协议 + 传输方式 + 安全机制组合，而不要直接假设配置能够跨实现移植。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Troubleshooting by Layer"
msgstr "按层排障"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "When a remote profile fails, debug from the bottom upward:"
msgstr "远程配置连接失败时，建议自底向上排查："

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "**Network reachability** — DNS, IP route, TCP/UDP port, firewall."
msgstr "**网络可达性** — DNS、IP 路由、TCP/UDP 端口、防火墙。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "**Transport security** — TLS certificate/SNI or REALITY key/short ID."
msgstr "**传输安全** — TLS 证书/SNI 或 REALITY 密钥/short ID。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "**Transport method** — RAW/WebSocket/XHTTP/QUIC settings."
msgstr "**传输方式** — RAW/WebSocket/XHTTP/QUIC 设置。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "**Proxy authentication** — password, UUID/user ID, Hysteria/TUIC auth."
msgstr "**代理认证** — 密码、UUID/用户 ID、Hysteria/TUIC 认证。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "**Destination routing** — rules, DNS mode, outbound group."
msgstr "**目标路由** — 规则、DNS 模式、出站组。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "**Advanced tuning** — multiplexing, congestion control, padding, custom headers, flow modes."
msgstr "**高级调优** — 多路复用、拥塞控制、padding、自定义请求头、flow 模式。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "Do not start by changing all six layers at once."
msgstr "不要一开始就同时修改所有六个层级。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[SOCKS5](./protocols/socks5.md) — standardized general-purpose TCP/UDP local proxy."
msgstr "[SOCKS5](./protocols/socks5.md) — 标准化的通用 TCP/UDP 本地代理。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[HTTP Proxy](./protocols/http.md) — application HTTP proxy and `CONNECT` tunneling."
msgstr "[HTTP 代理](./protocols/http.md) — 应用层 HTTP 代理与 `CONNECT` 隧道。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[Trojan](./protocols/trojan.md) — TLS-based password proxy with fallback behavior."
msgstr "[Trojan](./protocols/trojan.md) — 基于 TLS、使用密码认证并带有 fallback 行为的代理协议。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[Wire Format](./protocols/trojan/wire-format.md)"
msgstr "[报文格式](./protocols/trojan/wire-format.md)"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[Traffic Handling](./protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md)"
msgstr "[流量处理](./protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md)"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[Hysteria 2](./protocols/hysteria2.md) — QUIC-based TCP/UDP proxy with HTTP/3 authentication behavior."
msgstr "[Hysteria 2](./protocols/hysteria2.md) — 基于 QUIC、通过 HTTP/3 完成认证行为的 TCP/UDP 代理协议。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[TUIC](./protocols/tuic.md) — multiplexed low-latency TCP/UDP proxy protocol, commonly over QUIC."
msgstr "[TUIC](./protocols/tuic.md) — 通常运行在 QUIC 上、支持多路复用的低延迟 TCP/UDP 代理协议。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[VLESS](./protocols/vless.md) — lightweight Xray proxy protocol and identity layer."
msgstr "[VLESS](./protocols/vless.md) — 轻量级 Xray 代理协议与身份层。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[XHTTP Transport](./protocols/xhttp.md) — HTTP-oriented Xray transport method."
msgstr "[XHTTP 传输](./protocols/xhttp.md) — 面向 HTTP 的 Xray 传输方式。"

#: src\protocol.md
msgid "[REALITY](./protocols/reality.md) — Xray transport-security mechanism."
msgstr "[REALITY](./protocols/reality.md) — Xray 传输安全机制。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md src\protocols/http.md src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md src\protocols/vless.md src\protocols/xhttp.md src\protocols/reality.md
msgid "Positioning"
msgstr "定位"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "SOCKS5 is a general-purpose application proxy protocol standardized by RFC 1928. It can relay TCP connections and defines `UDP ASSOCIATE` for UDP traffic. Because SOCKS operates below HTTP semantics, applications can use it for many protocols without the proxy needing to understand the application payload."
msgstr "SOCKS5 是由 RFC 1928 标准化的通用应用代理协议。它可以转发 TCP 连接，并通过 `UDP ASSOCIATE` 定义 UDP 转发方式。由于 SOCKS 工作在 HTTP 语义之下，代理无需理解应用层载荷，就能被多种协议使用。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "For local Chimera deployments, SOCKS5 is usually the best baseline listener to validate before enabling TUN or transparent routing."
msgstr "对于本地 Chimera 部署，SOCKS5 通常是启用 TUN 或透明路由前最适合验证的基线监听器。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Standards"
msgstr "标准"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The main standards are:"
msgstr "主要相关标准包括："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 1928 — SOCKS Protocol Version 5."
msgstr "RFC 1928 — SOCKS Protocol Version 5。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 1929 — Username/Password Authentication for SOCKS V5."
msgstr "RFC 1929 — SOCKS V5 用户名/密码认证。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 1961 — GSS-API Authentication Method for SOCKS V5."
msgstr "RFC 1961 — SOCKS V5 的 GSS-API 认证方法。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 3089 — SOCKS-based IPv6/IPv4 Gateway operation."
msgstr "RFC 3089 — 基于 SOCKS 的 IPv6/IPv4 网关操作。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Protocol Flow"
msgstr "协议流程"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Method negotiation"
msgstr "方法协商"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The client opens a TCP connection to the SOCKS5 server."
msgstr "客户端先与 SOCKS5 服务端建立 TCP 连接。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The client sends the authentication methods it supports."
msgstr "客户端发送自己支持的认证方法列表。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The server chooses one method."
msgstr "服务端从中选择一种方法。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "If required, the client performs the selected authentication exchange."
msgstr "如有需要，客户端完成所选认证方式的交互。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Proxy request"
msgstr "代理请求"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "After negotiation, the client sends one of the SOCKS5 commands:"
msgstr "协商完成后，客户端发送以下某个 SOCKS5 命令："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`CONNECT` — create an outbound TCP connection."
msgstr "`CONNECT` — 创建出站 TCP 连接。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`BIND` — ask the proxy to accept a related incoming connection."
msgstr "`BIND` — 要求代理接受一个相关的入站连接。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`UDP ASSOCIATE` — establish the control association for UDP relay."
msgstr "`UDP ASSOCIATE` — 为 UDP 转发建立控制关联。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The request can identify a destination by IPv4 address, IPv6 address, or domain name."
msgstr "请求可以使用 IPv4 地址、IPv6 地址或域名来指定目标。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`CONNECT`"
msgstr "`CONNECT`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "For the common TCP case:"
msgstr "对于最常见的 TCP 场景："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The client asks the proxy to connect to a destination."
msgstr "客户端要求代理连接到目标地址。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The proxy evaluates access and routing policy."
msgstr "代理评估访问控制和路由策略。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The proxy returns a success or failure reply."
msgstr "代理返回成功或失败响应。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "After success, client and server relay the TCP byte stream."
msgstr "成功后，客户端与服务端开始双向转发 TCP 字节流。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`UDP ASSOCIATE`"
msgstr "`UDP ASSOCIATE`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "UDP relay uses the TCP SOCKS connection as the lifetime/control channel. The proxy returns an address and UDP port where the client sends SOCKS-framed UDP datagrams. The association ends when the corresponding TCP control connection ends."
msgstr "UDP 转发使用 SOCKS TCP 连接作为生命周期与控制通道。代理会返回一个地址和 UDP 端口，客户端把带 SOCKS 封装的 UDP 数据报发送到该端点。对应 TCP 控制连接结束时，这个关联也随之结束。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "UDP support is therefore a separate capability from basic SOCKS5 TCP support; do not assume that every SOCKS5 implementation supports it equally well."
msgstr "因此 UDP 支持是独立于基础 SOCKS5 TCP 支持的能力；不要假设所有 SOCKS5 实现对 UDP 的支持程度都相同。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Minimal Configuration"
msgstr "最小配置"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "A local `chimera_client`\\-style profile can start with:"
msgstr "本地 `chimera_client` 风格配置可以从下面的最小配置开始："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "An application can then use:"
msgstr "应用随后可以使用："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"socks5://127.0.0.1:7891\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"socks5://127.0.0.1:7891\n"
"```"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "When DNS behavior matters, distinguish between applications that resolve the domain locally and applications that pass the domain name to the SOCKS proxy. That difference can affect domain rules."
msgstr "当 DNS 行为会影响路由时，需要区分两类应用：一类先在本地解析域名，另一类把域名直接交给 SOCKS 代理解析。两者的差异会影响域名规则。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Generic TCP proxying without HTTP-specific assumptions."
msgstr "不依赖 HTTP 语义的通用 TCP 代理能力。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Domain-name, IPv4, and IPv6 destination forms."
msgstr "支持域名、IPv4 和 IPv6 三种目标地址形式。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Standardized UDP relay mechanism."
msgstr "标准化的 UDP 转发机制。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Widely supported by developer tools, browsers, SSH tooling, and networking libraries."
msgstr "被开发工具、浏览器、SSH 工具链以及网络库广泛支持。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Low protocol overhead and easy local debugging."
msgstr "协议开销低，本地调试简单。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "SOCKS5 itself does not provide transport encryption."
msgstr "SOCKS5 本身不提供传输加密。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Application support is required unless traffic is captured by another layer."
msgstr "除非由其他层捕获流量，否则应用本身必须支持 SOCKS5。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "UDP relay behavior can vary among clients, NATs, and proxy implementations."
msgstr "不同客户端、NAT 环境和代理实现之间的 UDP 转发行为可能存在差异。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Basic username/password authentication should not be treated as a substitute for encrypted transport."
msgstr "基础用户名/密码认证不能替代加密传输。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "DNS and Rule Interaction"
msgstr "DNS 与规则交互"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "SOCKS5 can preserve a domain name all the way to the proxy when the application uses remote resolution semantics. If the application resolves locally first, the proxy may only see the resulting IP address."
msgstr "当应用使用远程解析语义时，SOCKS5 可以一直把域名保留到代理端。如果应用先在本地完成解析，代理可能只能看到解析后的 IP 地址。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "This matters for rules such as:"
msgstr "这会直接影响类似下面的规则："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "DOMAIN-SUFFIX,example.com,Proxy"
msgstr "DOMAIN-SUFFIX,example.com,Proxy"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "If a domain rule unexpectedly stops matching, compare the application's DNS behavior with the client DNS mode described in [DNS Module](../chimera_client/dns.md)."
msgstr "如果域名规则意外停止命中，应将应用的 DNS 行为与 [DNS 模块](../chimera_client/dns.md) 中描述的客户端 DNS 模式进行对比。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md src\protocols/http.md src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md src\protocols/vless.md src\protocols/xhttp.md src\protocols/reality.md
msgid "Security Notes"
msgstr "安全说明"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "For desktop use, bind SOCKS5 to loopback unless LAN access is intentional. Publicly exposing an unauthenticated SOCKS listener creates an open-proxy risk. If remote SOCKS access is required, place it behind a secure authenticated channel rather than relying on SOCKS5 alone for confidentiality."
msgstr "桌面使用时，除非明确需要局域网访问，否则应把 SOCKS5 绑定到回环地址。把未认证的 SOCKS 监听器暴露到公网会产生开放代理风险。如果确实需要远程 SOCKS 访问，应将其置于安全且经过认证的通道之后，而不要只依赖 SOCKS5 本身提供机密性。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md src\protocols/http.md src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md src\protocols/vless.md src\protocols/xhttp.md src\protocols/reality.md
msgid "Chimera Status"
msgstr "Chimera 支持状态"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "SOCKS5 is documented as a current client-core inbound and is the recommended starting point for validating proxy profiles. Treat TCP `CONNECT` as the baseline capability; validate UDP association separately when an application requires UDP."
msgstr "当前文档将 SOCKS5 记录为客户端核心已有入站能力，并推荐将其作为验证代理配置的起点。应把 TCP `CONNECT` 视为基础能力；当应用需要 UDP 时，应单独验证 UDP association。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Chimera configures the listener through the selected core. It does not itself implement the SOCKS5 protocol."
msgstr "Chimera 通过当前选中的核心配置监听器，本身并不实现 SOCKS5 协议。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The current server capability map includes SOCKS-related inbound work. That is an implementation map rather than a guarantee of complete RFC 1928 parity, so server deployments should verify the commands and authentication modes they actually require."
msgstr "当前服务端能力地图包含 SOCKS 相关入站实现。它只是实现范围地图，并不保证完整达到 RFC 1928 一致性，因此服务端部署应验证实际需要的命令与认证方式。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Confirm the listener is bound to the expected address and port."
msgstr "确认监听器绑定到预期地址和端口。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Test a simple TCP destination before testing UDP."
msgstr "测试 UDP 前先验证一个简单 TCP 目标。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "If domain rules fail, determine whether the application sends a domain name or a pre-resolved IP address."
msgstr "如果域名规则失效，确认应用发送给代理的是域名还是预先解析好的 IP 地址。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "If authentication fails, test without authentication on loopback to isolate protocol behavior from credential configuration."
msgstr "如果认证失败，可以先在回环地址上关闭认证测试，以便把协议行为问题与凭据配置问题分开。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "For UDP failures, verify that the TCP control connection remains open and that local firewall/NAT rules allow the returned UDP relay endpoint."
msgstr "如果 UDP 失败，确认 TCP 控制连接仍保持打开，并检查本地防火墙/NAT 规则是否允许访问服务端返回的 UDP 转发端点。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "If SOCKS works but TUN does not, debug TUN routing separately rather than changing the proxy node configuration."
msgstr "如果 SOCKS 正常但 TUN 不通，应单独排查 TUN 路由，而不是修改代理节点配置。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 1928: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1928>"
msgstr "RFC 1928：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1928>"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 1929: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1929>"
msgstr "RFC 1929：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1929>"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 1961: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1961>"
msgstr "RFC 1961：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1961>"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 3089: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3089>"
msgstr "RFC 3089：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3089>"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "An HTTP proxy is an application-level proxy used by browsers, command-line tools, package managers, and operating-system proxy settings. For ordinary HTTP requests, the client sends the request through the proxy. For HTTPS and other TCP destinations, the client normally asks the proxy to create a tunnel with the HTTP `CONNECT` method."
msgstr "HTTP 代理是一种应用层代理，常用于浏览器、命令行工具、包管理器和操作系统代理设置。对于普通 HTTP 请求，客户端通过代理发送请求；对于 HTTPS 和其他 TCP 目标，客户端通常使用 HTTP `CONNECT` 方法要求代理建立隧道。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP proxying should not be confused with XHTTP. An HTTP proxy is an inbound proxy protocol used by local applications; [XHTTP](./xhttp.md) is an Xray transport used between compatible proxy endpoints."
msgstr "HTTP 代理不应与 XHTTP 混淆。HTTP 代理是本地应用使用的入站代理协议；[XHTTP](./xhttp.md) 则是兼容代理端点之间使用的一种 Xray 传输方式。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Plain HTTP request"
msgstr "普通 HTTP 请求"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The client connects to the HTTP proxy."
msgstr "客户端连接到 HTTP 代理。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The client sends a normal HTTP request using an absolute target URI."
msgstr "客户端使用绝对目标 URI 发送普通 HTTP 请求。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy applies authentication and routing policy."
msgstr "代理应用认证和路由策略。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy sends the request to the origin server and relays the response."
msgstr "代理把请求发送到源站，并把响应转发给客户端。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "`CONNECT` tunnel"
msgstr "`CONNECT` 隧道"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The client sends a request such as `CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1`."
msgstr "客户端发送类似 `CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1` 的请求。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy validates the target and access policy."
msgstr "代理验证目标和访问策略。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy establishes a TCP connection to the requested destination."
msgstr "代理与请求的目标建立 TCP 连接。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "After a successful response, the proxy relays bytes in both directions."
msgstr "返回成功响应后，代理开始双向转发字节流。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "For HTTPS, the end-to-end TLS handshake happens inside that tunnel."
msgstr "对于 HTTPS，端到端 TLS 握手会发生在该隧道内部。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The `CONNECT` method creates a TCP-oriented tunnel. It does not by itself add UDP proxying."
msgstr "`CONNECT` 方法创建的是面向 TCP 的隧道，本身并不会增加 UDP 代理能力。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Minimal Client-Side Configuration"
msgstr "最小客户端配置"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "A Clash-style local listener commonly looks like:"
msgstr "Clash 风格本地监听器通常类似："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "bind-address"
msgstr "bind-address"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "allow-lan"
msgstr "allow-lan"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Applications can then use:"
msgstr "应用随后可以使用："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"http://127.0.0.1:7890\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"http://127.0.0.1:7890\n"
"```"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "as their HTTP/HTTPS proxy endpoint."
msgstr "作为其 HTTP/HTTPS 代理端点。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The exact key names depend on the selected Chimera core. See [Ports and Listeners](../chimera_client/ports.md) for the current `chimera_client` mapping."
msgstr "具体配置键名称取决于当前选中的 Chimera 核心。`chimera_client` 的当前映射请参阅 [端口与监听器](../chimera_client/ports.md)。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP proxies may add an authentication layer, but authentication support varies by implementation. Common deployments use proxy-specific credentials or place the proxy behind another authenticated control plane."
msgstr "HTTP 代理可以增加认证层，但认证支持因实现而异。常见部署会使用代理专用凭据，或将代理置于另一个经过认证的控制层之后。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Do not assume that authentication also encrypts the connection between the application and the proxy. A plain local HTTP proxy has no transport encryption unless TLS or another secure channel is explicitly added."
msgstr "不要认为启用认证就等于加密应用与代理之间的连接。普通本地 HTTP 代理没有传输加密，除非显式加入 TLS 或其他安全通道。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Broad support in browsers, package managers, CLI tools, and operating systems."
msgstr "浏览器、包管理器、CLI 工具和操作系统广泛支持。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Simple to inspect and debug during local development."
msgstr "本地开发期间容易观察和调试。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTPS traffic can be tunneled without terminating the application's TLS session at the proxy."
msgstr "可以在不让代理终止应用 TLS 会话的情况下隧道转发 HTTPS 流量。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Well suited to local or trusted-LAN ingress into a proxy core."
msgstr "很适合作为本机或可信局域网进入代理核心的入站方式。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Primarily TCP-oriented; standard HTTP proxy behavior does not provide general UDP relay."
msgstr "主要面向 TCP；标准 HTTP 代理行为不提供通用 UDP 转发。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "A clear-text proxy listener is unsuitable for direct exposure to the public internet."
msgstr "明文代理监听器不适合直接暴露到公网。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Applications that ignore operating-system proxy settings will bypass it."
msgstr "忽略操作系统代理设置的应用会绕过它。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Authentication and header behavior vary across implementations."
msgstr "不同实现的认证和请求头行为可能不同。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "For a local desktop deployment, prefer binding the HTTP listener to `127.0.0.1`. If LAN access is enabled, apply an explicit firewall policy and understand which clients can reach the proxy."
msgstr "本地桌面部署应优先把 HTTP 监听器绑定到 `127.0.0.1`。如果启用了局域网访问，应配置明确的防火墙策略，并清楚哪些客户端可以访问代理。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Exposing an unauthenticated HTTP proxy publicly can turn the host into an open proxy. Even when authentication is enabled, a plain HTTP connection can expose credentials or metadata to observers on the local network."
msgstr "把未认证 HTTP 代理公开暴露可能使主机变成开放代理。即使启用了认证，明文 HTTP 连接仍可能向本地网络观察者暴露凭据或元数据。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The current Wiki documents an HTTP listener as part of the client-core inbound surface. Availability can still depend on the selected build, configuration, and runtime path. Validate HTTP `CONNECT` behavior with a minimal profile before combining it with TUN, DNS hijacking, or complex rules."
msgstr "当前 Wiki 将 HTTP 监听器记录为客户端核心入站接口的一部分。是否实际可用仍可能取决于构建版本、配置和运行时路径。在与 TUN、DNS 劫持或复杂规则组合之前，应先使用最小配置验证 HTTP `CONNECT` 行为。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Chimera itself does not implement HTTP proxying. It configures and manages the selected core, so listener behavior follows that core."
msgstr "Chimera 本身不实现 HTTP 代理，而是配置和管理当前选中的核心，因此监听器行为由该核心决定。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP proxying is mainly relevant as a local/client-side inbound. Server-side HTTP capabilities should be treated separately from remote encrypted proxy protocols such as Trojan, Hysteria 2, or VLESS."
msgstr "HTTP 代理主要作为本地/客户端侧入站使用。服务端 HTTP 能力应与 Trojan、Hysteria 2、VLESS 等远程加密代理协议分开理解。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "If a browser or CLI tool cannot connect:"
msgstr "如果浏览器或 CLI 工具无法连接："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Verify the listener address and port."
msgstr "检查监听地址和端口。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Confirm the process is listening on the expected interface."
msgstr "确认进程正在预期网络接口上监听。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Test a simple HTTP request before testing HTTPS."
msgstr "测试 HTTPS 前先验证一个简单 HTTP 请求。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "For HTTPS failures, confirm that `CONNECT` reaches the proxy and that the target host/port is allowed."
msgstr "如果 HTTPS 失败，确认 `CONNECT` 已经到达代理，并且目标主机/端口被允许访问。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Check authentication separately from routing rules."
msgstr "将认证问题与路由规则问题分开检查。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "If only some applications fail, verify that those applications actually use the configured system proxy."
msgstr "如果只有部分应用失败，确认这些应用确实使用了已经配置的系统代理。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "RFC 9110, HTTP Semantics: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110>"
msgstr "RFC 9110，HTTP Semantics：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110>"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Xray HTTP inbound reference: <https://xtls.github.io/en/config/inbounds/http.html>"
msgstr "Xray HTTP 入站参考：<https://xtls.github.io/en/config/inbounds/http.html>"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Trojan is a TLS-based proxy protocol designed so that the outer connection uses a normal TLS session while proxy authentication and destination metadata are carried inside encrypted application data."
msgstr "Trojan 是一种基于 TLS 的代理协议。其外层连接使用普通 TLS 会话，而代理认证信息和目标元数据则封装在加密后的应用数据中。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The original Trojan protocol uses a pre-shared password, represented on the wire as the hexadecimal SHA-224 digest of that password. Its request address format is similar to SOCKS5 and supports both TCP `CONNECT` and UDP association."
msgstr "原始 Trojan 协议使用预共享密码，在报文中以该密码的 SHA-224 摘要十六进制形式表示。其请求地址格式与 SOCKS5 类似，同时支持 TCP `CONNECT` 和 UDP association。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The baseline protocol described here should be distinguished from additional transport combinations exposed by individual proxy cores, such as WebSocket, XHTTP, or other wrappers."
msgstr "这里描述的是基础 Trojan 协议，应与各代理核心额外提供的 WebSocket、XHTTP 或其他封装传输组合区分开。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/vless.md src\protocols/reality.md
msgid "Connection Flow"
msgstr "连接流程"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The client opens a TCP connection to the Trojan server."
msgstr "客户端与 Trojan 服务端建立 TCP 连接。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Client and server complete a normal TLS handshake."
msgstr "客户端与服务端完成普通 TLS 握手。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Inside TLS application data, the client sends the password digest and Trojan request header."
msgstr "在 TLS 应用数据中，客户端发送密码摘要和 Trojan 请求头。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The server validates the password and destination request."
msgstr "服务端验证密码和目标请求。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "For TCP, the server connects to the target and relays the stream."
msgstr "对于 TCP，服务端连接目标并转发字节流。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "For UDP, datagrams are framed inside the Trojan TLS stream."
msgstr "对于 UDP，数据报会被封装在 Trojan TLS 流中。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Invalid traffic can be handled by a fallback service instead of exposing a proxy-specific response."
msgstr "无效流量可以交给 fallback 服务处理，而不是返回容易暴露代理特征的专用响应。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The detailed byte layout is documented in [Wire Format](./trojan/wire-format.md). Fallback behavior is discussed in [Traffic Handling](./trojan/traffic-handling.md)."
msgstr "详细字节布局请参阅 [报文格式](./trojan/wire-format.md)。Fallback 行为请参阅 [流量处理](./trojan/traffic-handling.md)。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Minimal Deployment Model"
msgstr "最小部署模型"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "A practical deployment needs at least:"
msgstr "一个实际可用的部署至少需要："

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "a TCP listening address and port,"
msgstr "TCP 监听地址和端口；"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "TLS certificate/key or another implementation-specific TLS termination path,"
msgstr "TLS 证书/密钥，或实现所支持的其他 TLS 终止方式；"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "one or more Trojan passwords,"
msgstr "一个或多个 Trojan 密码；"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "a fallback policy if camouflage behavior is desired,"
msgstr "如果需要伪装行为，还需要 fallback 策略；"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "and routing rules for outbound traffic."
msgstr "以及出站流量的路由规则。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "A conceptual client entry looks like:"
msgstr "概念性的客户端配置类似："

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "trojan-example"
msgstr "trojan-example"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "trojan"
msgstr "trojan"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md src\protocols/vless.md src\protocols/xhttp.md src\protocols/reality.md
msgid "proxy.example.com"
msgstr "proxy.example.com"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md
msgid "password"
msgstr "password"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md
msgid "\"CHANGE-ME\""
msgstr "\"CHANGE-ME\""

#: src\protocols/trojan.md src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md
msgid "sni"
msgstr "sni"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Exact transport keys vary by selected core. If WebSocket or another transport is enabled, both endpoints must use compatible transport settings."
msgstr "具体传输配置键会因所选核心而异。如果启用了 WebSocket 或其他传输方式，两端必须使用兼容的传输设置。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The original protocol uses a shared secret. A server can assign different passwords to different users, but credential lifecycle is still application configuration rather than a negotiated identity system."
msgstr "原始协议使用共享密钥。服务端可以给不同用户分配不同密码，但凭据生命周期仍属于应用配置，而不是通过协议协商形成的身份系统。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Operationally:"
msgstr "运维上建议："

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "use unique, high-entropy credentials,"
msgstr "使用唯一且高熵的凭据；"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "avoid reusing a password across unrelated servers,"
msgstr "避免在无关服务器之间复用密码；"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "rotate credentials when a client is decommissioned,"
msgstr "客户端停用后及时轮换凭据；"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "and do not expose credentials in logs or example configs."
msgstr "不要在日志或示例配置中暴露凭据。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "TLS Requirements"
msgstr "TLS 要求"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Trojan depends heavily on the quality of its TLS deployment. The certificate, SNI behavior, ALPN configuration, and fallback endpoint should be internally consistent."
msgstr "Trojan 高度依赖 TLS 部署质量。证书、SNI 行为、ALPN 配置和 fallback 端点应保持一致、相互匹配。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "For the original TLS-camouflage design, a valid and ordinary-looking HTTPS configuration is preferable to an obviously synthetic endpoint."
msgstr "对于原始 TLS 伪装设计，应优先使用有效且看起来正常的 HTTPS 配置，而不是明显人为构造的端点。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "TCP and UDP"
msgstr "TCP 与 UDP"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "TCP requests are straightforward after authentication: the server opens the requested destination and relays bytes in both directions."
msgstr "认证成功后，TCP 请求的处理较直接：服务端连接所请求的目标，并双向转发字节流。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "UDP traffic is encapsulated in per-datagram Trojan framing carried over the TLS stream. This differs from QUIC-native protocols such as Hysteria 2 and TUIC, which can use QUIC datagrams."
msgstr "UDP 流量以逐数据报的 Trojan 封装承载在 TLS 流中。这与 Hysteria 2、TUIC 等 QUIC 原生协议不同，后者可以使用 QUIC Datagram。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Uses mature TLS implementations for confidentiality and server identity."
msgstr "利用成熟 TLS 实现提供机密性和服务端身份验证。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Small protocol-specific framing after TLS establishment."
msgstr "TLS 建立后，协议自身封装开销较小。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Supports both TCP and UDP relay in the baseline protocol."
msgstr "基础协议同时支持 TCP 与 UDP 转发。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Invalid requests can be sent to a normal fallback service instead of a proxy-specific error page."
msgstr "无效请求可以转发到普通 fallback 服务，而不是返回代理专用错误页面。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Familiar certificate-based operations for administrators already running HTTPS services."
msgstr "对于已经维护 HTTPS 服务的管理员，证书相关运维方式较为熟悉。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Certificate issuance and renewal become part of server operations unless the selected stack provides another compatible security mechanism."
msgstr "除非所选技术栈提供其他兼容安全机制，否则证书签发与续期会成为服务端日常运维的一部分。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Shared-secret authentication requires deliberate credential management."
msgstr "共享密钥认证需要认真管理凭据生命周期。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "TLS camouflage is only as convincing as the surrounding TLS and fallback configuration."
msgstr "TLS 伪装效果取决于周边 TLS 与 fallback 配置是否自然一致。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "UDP is tunneled through the TLS/TCP-oriented connection model rather than using a native unreliable datagram transport."
msgstr "UDP 通过面向 TLS/TCP 的连接模型进行隧道封装，而不是使用原生不可靠数据报传输。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Do not disable certificate verification in production merely to make a test configuration connect. A successful TCP connection with invalid TLS validation is not equivalent to a secure deployment."
msgstr "不要为了让测试配置连通就在生产环境关闭证书验证。TCP 能连接但 TLS 验证无效，并不等于安全部署。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Fallbacks also need care. A fallback should not unintentionally expose private services, administrative endpoints, or internal-only content."
msgstr "Fallback 同样需要谨慎配置，不能意外暴露私有服务、管理端点或仅供内部访问的内容。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The current Wiki lists **Trojan + WebSocket** among the client-core capabilities. Because the original Trojan protocol and an implementation-specific WebSocket transport are separate layers, verify both the Trojan credentials and transport options when troubleshooting."
msgstr "当前 Wiki 将 **Trojan + WebSocket** 列为客户端核心能力之一。由于原始 Trojan 协议与实现特定的 WebSocket 传输属于不同层级，排障时应同时验证 Trojan 凭据和传输选项。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Chimera manages the selected core and profile. Trojan protocol behavior belongs to that core rather than the GUI itself."
msgstr "Chimera 负责管理所选核心和配置文件；Trojan 协议行为属于代理核心，而不是 GUI 本身。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "The server capability map includes Trojan-related inbound parsing/handling. Treat this as current implementation scope, not automatic compatibility with every Trojan client or every optional transport combination."
msgstr "服务端能力地图包含 Trojan 相关入站解析/处理。这里表示的是当前实现范围，并不意味着自动兼容所有 Trojan 客户端或所有可选传输组合。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Confirm DNS resolves the intended server address."
msgstr "确认 DNS 解析到了预期服务器地址。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Verify TCP reachability to the server port."
msgstr "确认服务端端口的 TCP 可达性。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Validate certificate trust, SNI, and system time."
msgstr "检查证书信任、SNI 和系统时间。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Check the Trojan password independently of transport-specific options."
msgstr "将 Trojan 密码与传输特定选项分开检查。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "If WebSocket is used, verify path/Host/header settings on both endpoints."
msgstr "如果使用 WebSocket，检查两端的 path/Host/header 设置。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "If authentication fails but HTTPS fallback works, inspect credential and Trojan request configuration rather than the TLS listener itself."
msgstr "如果认证失败但 HTTPS fallback 正常，应检查凭据和 Trojan 请求配置，而不是先怀疑 TLS 监听器本身。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "For UDP issues, first confirm TCP Trojan traffic works and then test UDP as a separate capability."
msgstr "如果 UDP 有问题，先确认 Trojan TCP 流量正常，再把 UDP 作为独立能力进行测试。"

#: src\protocols/trojan.md
msgid "Trojan protocol documentation: <https://trojan-gfw.github.io/trojan/protocol.html>"
msgstr "Trojan 协议文档：<https://trojan-gfw.github.io/trojan/protocol.html>"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "范围"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "This page documents the baseline Trojan protocol framing after the TLS session has been established. Transport wrappers added by individual implementations can add another layer around this baseline and should be documented separately."
msgstr "本页记录 TLS 会话建立后基础 Trojan 协议的封装格式。不同实现添加的传输封装可能会在此基础上再增加一层，应当单独记录。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "1. TLS Handshake"
msgstr "1. TLS 握手"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Trojan starts with a normal TLS handshake. Only after TLS succeeds does the client send Trojan authentication and destination information."
msgstr "Trojan 从普通 TLS 握手开始。只有 TLS 成功建立后，客户端才会发送 Trojan 认证信息和目标信息。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "If the TLS handshake fails, there is no valid Trojan application session. A server may also provide ordinary HTTPS behavior for non-Trojan traffic as part of its fallback design."
msgstr "如果 TLS 握手失败，就不存在有效的 Trojan 应用会话。作为 fallback 设计的一部分，服务端也可以对非 Trojan 流量提供普通 HTTPS 行为。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "2. Initial Application Request"
msgstr "2. 初始应用请求"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "The first Trojan application data has this logical form:"
msgstr "第一段 Trojan 应用数据在逻辑上具有以下结构："

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "The 56-byte authentication field is the lowercase/uppercase-insensitive hex representation of the 28-byte SHA-224 digest, as expected by the implementation. The exact credential handling should follow the endpoint implementation rather than relying on manual hashing in normal user configuration."
msgstr "56 字节认证字段是 28 字节 SHA-224 摘要的十六进制表示，大小写处理以具体实现要求为准。正常用户配置应遵循端点实现的凭据处理方式，而不是依赖手工计算哈希。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "The optional initial payload allows the client to send application data in the same logical request instead of waiting for an additional round trip."
msgstr "可选的初始 payload 允许客户端在同一个逻辑请求中直接发送应用数据，从而避免再等待一次额外往返。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "3. Trojan Request"
msgstr "3. Trojan 请求"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "The request reuses a SOCKS5-like destination format:"
msgstr "请求复用了类似 SOCKS5 的目标地址格式："

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`CMD`"
msgstr "`CMD`"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Value"
msgstr "值"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`0x01`"
msgstr "`0x01`"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "TCP `CONNECT`"
msgstr "TCP `CONNECT`"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`0x03`"
msgstr "`0x03`"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "UDP association"
msgstr "UDP association"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`ATYP`"
msgstr "`ATYP`"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Address form"
msgstr "地址形式"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "IPv4"
msgstr "IPv4"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Domain name"
msgstr "域名"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`0x04`"
msgstr "`0x04`"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "IPv6"
msgstr "IPv6"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`DST.PORT` is encoded in network byte order."
msgstr "`DST.PORT` 使用网络字节序编码。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "For address-field semantics, SOCKS5 RFC 1928 is a useful reference because the Trojan request intentionally follows the same general address model."
msgstr "在理解地址字段语义时，SOCKS5 RFC 1928 是很有价值的参考，因为 Trojan 请求有意采用了相同的通用地址模型。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "4. TCP Payload"
msgstr "4. TCP Payload"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "For a valid TCP request, bytes following the second CRLF can immediately become payload for the requested destination. After the request has been accepted, subsequent application data is relayed through the TLS connection."
msgstr "对于有效 TCP 请求，第二个 CRLF 之后的字节可以立即作为目标连接的 payload。请求被接受后，后续应用数据通过 TLS 连接持续转发。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Conceptually:"
msgstr "概念上可以表示为："

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "5. UDP Datagram Framing"
msgstr "5. UDP 数据报封装"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "For UDP association, each UDP datagram is framed separately inside the TLS stream:"
msgstr "对于 UDP association，每个 UDP 数据报都在 TLS 流中单独封装："

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`ATYP`, `DST.ADDR`, and `DST.PORT` identify the UDP destination."
msgstr "`ATYP`、`DST.ADDR` 和 `DST.PORT` 用于标识 UDP 目标。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`Length` is the UDP payload length in network byte order."
msgstr "`Length` 是以网络字节序表示的 UDP payload 长度。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "`Payload` is one UDP datagram."
msgstr "`Payload` 表示一个 UDP 数据报。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Because UDP datagrams are carried inside a TLS stream, packet boundaries are represented by this framing rather than by the underlying transport."
msgstr "由于 UDP 数据报承载在 TLS 字节流中，数据报边界需要由这层封装表示，而不能依赖底层传输自身的包边界。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "6. Parser Considerations"
msgstr "6. 解析器注意事项"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "An implementation should treat the request as structured binary data rather than assuming a single socket read contains the entire header. TLS and TCP can split application data across reads."
msgstr "实现应把请求视为结构化二进制数据，而不能假设一次 socket 读取就会获得完整请求头。TLS 和 TCP 都可能把应用数据拆分到多次读取中。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Important parser checks include:"
msgstr "解析器需要重点检查："

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "complete 56-byte authentication field,"
msgstr "完整的 56 字节认证字段；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "exact CRLF delimiters,"
msgstr "精确的 CRLF 分隔符；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "valid `CMD`,"
msgstr "有效的 `CMD`；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "supported `ATYP`,"
msgstr "受支持的 `ATYP`；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "bounded domain-name and payload lengths,"
msgstr "受限且合理的域名与 payload 长度；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "complete destination port,"
msgstr "完整的目标端口字段；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "and complete UDP payload before dispatch."
msgstr "以及在分发前确保 UDP payload 完整。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Malformed input should not panic the server or expose protocol-specific debug information to an unauthenticated peer."
msgstr "畸形输入不应导致服务端 panic，也不应向未认证对端暴露协议特定调试信息。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "7. Relationship to Chimera"
msgstr "7. 与 Chimera 的关系"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "This wire format is the baseline Trojan reference. `Chimera_Client` currently documents Trojan together with WebSocket support, so a deployed connection may contain an additional transport layer around the Trojan payload. Likewise, `Chimera_Server` compatibility should be tested against the exact transport and framing combination being used."
msgstr "该报文格式是基础 Trojan 参考。`Chimera_Client` 当前把 Trojan 与 WebSocket 支持一起记录，因此实际部署连接可能在 Trojan payload 外还有额外传输层。同样，`Chimera_Server` 的兼容性也应针对实际使用的传输与封装组合进行验证。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "Trojan protocol: <https://trojan-gfw.github.io/trojan/protocol.html>"
msgstr "Trojan 协议：<https://trojan-gfw.github.io/trojan/protocol.html>"

#: src\protocols/trojan/wire-format.md
msgid "SOCKS5 address model: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1928>"
msgstr "SOCKS5 地址模型：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1928>"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x00` — no authentication."
msgstr "`0x00` — 无需认证。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x02` — username/password authentication defined by RFC 1929."
msgstr "`0x02` — RFC 1929 定义的用户名/密码认证。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0xff` — no acceptable method."
msgstr "`0xff` — 没有可接受的认证方法。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`REP` communicates the result. RFC 1928 defines these one-byte values:"
msgstr "`REP` 用于表示请求结果。RFC 1928 定义了以下单字节取值："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`REP`"
msgstr "`REP`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x00`"
msgstr "`0x00`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "succeeded"
msgstr "成功"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "general SOCKS server failure"
msgstr "SOCKS 服务器常规故障"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "connection not allowed by ruleset"
msgstr "规则集不允许该连接"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "network unreachable"
msgstr "网络不可达"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "host unreachable"
msgstr "主机不可达"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x05`"
msgstr "`0x05`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "connection refused"
msgstr "连接被拒绝"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x06`"
msgstr "`0x06`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "TTL expired"
msgstr "TTL 已过期"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x07`"
msgstr "`0x07`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "command not supported"
msgstr "不支持该命令"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x08`"
msgstr "`0x08`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "address type not supported"
msgstr "不支持该地址类型"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`0x09`\\-`0xff`"
msgstr "`0x09`\\-`0xff`"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "unassigned"
msgstr "未分配"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "For a failed request, RFC 1928 requires the SOCKS server to close the TCP connection shortly after sending the reply. A client should therefore treat a non-zero `REP` as terminal for that request instead of waiting for a later application payload."
msgstr "对于失败请求，RFC 1928 要求 SOCKS 服务器在发送回复后不久关闭 TCP 连接。因此客户端应把非零 `REP` 视为该请求的终止结果，而不是继续等待后续应用层负载。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`BIND`: two replies, not one"
msgstr "`BIND`：不是一次，而是两次回复"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`BIND` is unusual because one request can produce **two successful server replies**. It was designed for protocols in which the proxied application expects a peer to connect back to it."
msgstr "`BIND` 的特殊之处在于，一个请求可能产生**两次成功的服务端回复**。它用于被代理应用需要等待对端反向建立连接的协议场景。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The first `BND.ADDR/BND.PORT` is the listening endpoint created by the SOCKS server. The second identifies the remote peer after the inbound connection is accepted. This is materially different from `CONNECT`, where one success reply is enough to enter the relay state."
msgstr "第一次回复中的 `BND.ADDR/BND.PORT` 是 SOCKS 服务器创建的监听端点；第二次回复则在入站连接被接受后标识实际连接进来的远端对端。这与 `CONNECT` 明显不同，后者一次成功回复即可进入转发状态。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "An implementation state machine therefore needs a distinct `BIND_WAIT_PEER` state rather than treating every `REP=0x00` as permission to begin application relay immediately."
msgstr "因此实现状态机需要单独的 `BIND_WAIT_PEER` 状态，不能把每个 `REP=0x00` 都理解为可以立即开始应用数据转发。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`UDP ASSOCIATE` datagram wire format"
msgstr "`UDP ASSOCIATE` 数据报线格式"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`UDP ASSOCIATE` uses the TCP SOCKS connection only as the control/lifetime channel. UDP payloads themselves use a separate SOCKS5 UDP header:"
msgstr "`UDP ASSOCIATE` 只把 TCP SOCKS 连接作为控制与生命周期通道；UDP 负载本身使用独立的 SOCKS5 UDP 头："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Fields:"
msgstr "字段："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`RSV` is two zero bytes (`0x0000`)."
msgstr "`RSV` 为两个零字节（`0x0000`）。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`FRAG=0x00` means the datagram is not fragmented."
msgstr "`FRAG=0x00` 表示该数据报未分片。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`ATYP`, `DST.ADDR`, and `DST.PORT` use the same destination-address model as the TCP request command."
msgstr "`ATYP`、`DST.ADDR` 和 `DST.PORT` 使用与 TCP 请求命令相同的目标地址模型。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "`DATA` is exactly one application UDP datagram payload."
msgstr "`DATA` 恰好对应一个应用层 UDP 数据报的负载。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The important boundary property is that UDP itself already preserves datagram boundaries. SOCKS5 therefore prepends routing metadata to **each UDP datagram** instead of turning all UDP traffic into one byte stream."
msgstr "一个关键的边界特性是 UDP 本身就保留数据报边界。因此 SOCKS5 会在**每个 UDP 数据报**前附加路由元数据，而不是把所有 UDP 流量转换成单一字节流。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Fragmentation semantics"
msgstr "分片语义"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "RFC 1928 defines a SOCKS-layer fragmentation mechanism through `FRAG`, but also states that an implementation may choose not to support it. An implementation that does not support fragmentation must drop any datagram whose `FRAG` field is not zero."
msgstr "RFC 1928 通过 `FRAG` 定义了 SOCKS 层分片机制，但同时允许实现选择不支持该机制。不支持分片的实现必须丢弃所有 `FRAG` 字段非零的数据报。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "When fragmentation is implemented, the low seven bits carry the fragment sequence number and the high bit marks the final fragment. Reassembly has a short expiration timer and a fragment arriving with a lower sequence number than the highest already seen causes the reassembly queue to be discarded."
msgstr "实现分片时，低七位携带分片序号，最高位用于标记最后一个分片。重组具有较短的过期计时器；如果收到的分片序号低于此前见到的最高序号，应丢弃当前重组队列。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "This makes SOCKS5 fragmentation very different from protocols such as Hysteria 2 or TUIC, whose fragment headers explicitly carry packet/session identifiers and fragment counts."
msgstr "这使 SOCKS5 分片与 Hysteria 2、TUIC 等协议明显不同：后者的分片头会显式携带数据包/会话标识以及分片数量。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "UDP association lifecycle and source binding"
msgstr "UDP 关联生命周期与源端绑定"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The client first sends a normal TCP `UDP ASSOCIATE` request. A successful reply returns `BND.ADDR/BND.PORT`, the UDP relay endpoint to which the client sends SOCKS5 UDP datagrams."
msgstr "客户端首先通过 TCP 发送普通的 `UDP ASSOCIATE` 请求。成功回复会返回 `BND.ADDR/BND.PORT`，客户端随后把 SOCKS5 UDP 数据报发送到这个 UDP 中继端点。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The TCP connection is the association's lifetime anchor: once it closes, the UDP association terminates. RFC 1928 also requires the server to restrict relay traffic to the client associated with that TCP request rather than behaving as an unrestricted public UDP forwarder."
msgstr "TCP 连接是该关联的生命周期锚点：一旦 TCP 连接关闭，UDP 关联也随之终止。RFC 1928 还要求服务器只为与该 TCP 请求关联的客户端转发流量，而不能充当不受限制的公共 UDP 转发器。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The client may put all-zero address/port values in the request when it does not know the UDP source endpoint at request time. The server reply, not the request, is the authoritative destination for the client's SOCKS-encapsulated UDP traffic."
msgstr "如果客户端在请求时还不知道自己的 UDP 源端点，可以在请求中填入全零地址/端口。对于客户端封装后的 SOCKS UDP 流量，真正权威的发送目标是服务端回复，而不是请求中的地址。"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Control/data state machine"
msgstr "控制面/数据面状态机"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "The complete baseline state machine is therefore:"
msgstr "因此完整的基准状态机如下："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Packet-capture view"
msgstr "抓包视角"

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "SOCKS5 is unencrypted unless the selected authentication method adds its own encapsulation. A normal packet capture can therefore expose the protocol phases directly:"
msgstr "除非选定的认证方法额外提供封装，否则 SOCKS5 本身不加密。因此普通抓包通常可以直接看到各协议阶段："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "For UDP, the capture additionally shows independent UDP packets beginning with `00 00 FRAG ATYP ...`. This clear separation between a TCP control association and a UDP data plane is one of the most useful reference points when comparing SOCKS5 with QUIC-native proxy protocols."
msgstr "对于 UDP，抓包还会看到以 `00 00 FRAG ATYP ...` 开头的独立 UDP 数据包。TCP 控制关联与 UDP 数据面的这种明确分离，是比较 SOCKS5 与 QUIC 原生代理协议时最有价值的基准之一。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Trojan's outer TLS behavior is only part of its deployment model. The server also needs a deliberate policy for traffic that reaches the TLS listener but is not a valid Trojan request."
msgstr "Trojan 的外层 TLS 行为只是部署模型的一部分。服务端还需要明确规定：到达 TLS 监听器但不是有效 Trojan 请求的流量应该如何处理。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "A well-designed fallback path serves two goals:"
msgstr "设计良好的 fallback 路径主要实现两个目标："

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "ordinary HTTPS/non-Trojan traffic receives ordinary service behavior,"
msgstr "普通 HTTPS/非 Trojan 流量得到普通服务行为；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "invalid proxy authentication does not produce an obvious proxy-specific banner."
msgstr "无效代理认证不会产生明显的代理专用响应特征。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Valid Trojan Traffic"
msgstr "有效 Trojan 流量"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "After TLS completes, a valid client sends the Trojan authentication field and a well-formed request. The server validates both before opening the requested outbound connection."
msgstr "TLS 建立后，有效客户端会发送 Trojan 认证字段和格式正确的请求。服务端验证二者后，才建立请求的出站连接。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "For valid traffic:"
msgstr "对于有效流量："

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Non-Trojan Traffic"
msgstr "非 Trojan 流量"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "The original Trojan design allows traffic that is not recognized as a valid Trojan request to be passed to a configured fallback endpoint."
msgstr "原始 Trojan 设计允许把无法识别为有效 Trojan 请求的流量转发到预先配置的 fallback 端点。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "The fallback service might be a local web server or another deliberately configured endpoint. Its job is to return the normal application behavior that an unauthenticated visitor should see."
msgstr "Fallback 服务可以是本地 Web 服务器，也可以是其他明确配置的端点。它的职责是返回未认证访问者正常情况下应该看到的应用行为。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Why Fallback Behavior Matters"
msgstr "为什么 Fallback 行为很重要"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Without a fallback, malformed input may receive a connection reset or a protocol-specific response that differs from the surrounding HTTPS service. That makes the endpoint easier to distinguish operationally."
msgstr "如果没有 fallback，畸形输入可能得到连接重置或与周围 HTTPS 服务不同的协议专用响应，这会让端点在行为上更容易被区分。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "A fallback does not make a server \"undetectable\". It simply avoids unnecessary behavioral differences for traffic that is not accepted as Trojan."
msgstr "Fallback 并不会让服务端变得“不可检测”。它只是避免对未被接受为 Trojan 的流量表现出不必要的异常行为差异。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Security Boundaries"
msgstr "安全边界"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Fallback forwarding must be treated as a security-sensitive routing rule. Avoid forwarding unauthenticated traffic to:"
msgstr "Fallback 转发必须被视为安全敏感的路由规则。不要把未认证流量转发到："

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "internal dashboards,"
msgstr "内部控制面板；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "metadata services,"
msgstr "元数据服务；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "databases,"
msgstr "数据库；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "administrative HTTP endpoints,"
msgstr "管理用 HTTP 端点；"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "or arbitrary private-network destinations."
msgstr "或任意私网目标。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Prefer a dedicated low-privilege web service whose public behavior is expected and safe."
msgstr "建议使用专门的低权限 Web 服务，并确保其公开行为符合预期且安全。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Certificate and SNI Consistency"
msgstr "证书与 SNI 一致性"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "The TLS certificate, configured SNI, fallback content, and public DNS name should tell a coherent story. For example, a certificate for one hostname with a fallback page that redirects to an unrelated private domain is operationally confusing and can make troubleshooting harder."
msgstr "TLS 证书、配置的 SNI、fallback 内容和公网 DNS 名称应保持逻辑一致。例如，证书属于一个主机名，而 fallback 页面却重定向到无关的私有域名，会让部署行为显得混乱，也会增加排障难度。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Reverse Proxy Deployments"
msgstr "反向代理部署"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "If Nginx, Caddy, or another reverse proxy is part of the path, document clearly which component terminates TLS and which component sees the Trojan application payload. The original Trojan framing assumes the Trojan endpoint receives the post-TLS byte stream."
msgstr "如果链路中包含 Nginx、Caddy 或其他反向代理，应清楚记录哪个组件负责终止 TLS、哪个组件能够看到 Trojan 应用 payload。原始 Trojan 封装假定 Trojan 端点直接接收 TLS 解密后的字节流。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Transport wrappers such as WebSocket introduce another routing layer and should not be treated as identical to the original direct-TLS layout."
msgstr "WebSocket 等传输封装会额外引入一层路由，不应把它与原始直连 TLS 布局视为完全相同。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Operational Checks"
msgstr "运维检查"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "When validating a deployment, test both accepted and rejected traffic:"
msgstr "验证部署时，应同时测试被接受和被拒绝的流量："

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "A valid Trojan client can authenticate and reach a known destination."
msgstr "有效 Trojan 客户端能够完成认证并访问已知目标。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "An invalid password does not reach the proxy destination."
msgstr "无效密码不能访问代理目标。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Ordinary HTTPS/non-Trojan traffic reaches the intended fallback."
msgstr "普通 HTTPS/非 Trojan 流量能够到达预期 fallback。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "The fallback cannot access sensitive private services."
msgstr "Fallback 无法访问敏感私有服务。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Logs distinguish operational failures for administrators without leaking useful authentication details to remote clients."
msgstr "日志应当帮助管理员区分各类运行故障，同时不能向远程客户端泄露有价值的认证细节。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Chimera Notes"
msgstr "Chimera 说明"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "`Chimera_Client` currently documents Trojan together with WebSocket support, so its traffic path can differ from the original direct-TLS Trojan deployment. `Chimera_Server` should likewise be tested against the exact inbound transport configuration in use."
msgstr "`Chimera_Client` 当前把 Trojan 与 WebSocket 支持一起记录，因此其流量路径可能与原始直连 TLS Trojan 部署不同。`Chimera_Server` 同样应针对实际使用的入站传输配置进行测试。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "This page therefore describes the baseline fallback model, not a guarantee that every Chimera transport combination uses the same fallback mechanism."
msgstr "因此，本页描述的是基础 fallback 模型，并不保证所有 Chimera 传输组合都使用完全相同的 fallback 机制。"

#: src\protocols/trojan/traffic-handling.md
msgid "Trojan protocol and fallback behavior: <https://trojan-gfw.github.io/trojan/protocol.html>"
msgstr "Trojan 协议与 fallback 行为：<https://trojan-gfw.github.io/trojan/protocol.html>"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 is a TCP and UDP proxy protocol built on QUIC. Its design combines QUIC streams for reliable TCP-style proxying, QUIC datagrams for UDP relay, TLS security from QUIC, and an HTTP/3-facing authentication path intended to make an unauthenticated endpoint behave like an ordinary HTTP/3 service."
msgstr "Hysteria 2 是构建在 QUIC 之上的 TCP 与 UDP 代理协议。其设计结合了用于可靠 TCP 风格代理的 QUIC Stream、用于 UDP 转发的 QUIC Datagram、QUIC 自带的 TLS 安全能力，以及面向 HTTP/3 的认证路径，使未认证端点可以表现得更像普通 HTTP/3 服务。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 is especially relevant on paths where packet loss or high latency makes conventional TCP-over-TCP-style designs perform poorly. It is not a universal replacement for TCP-based protocols: the network must permit stable UDP/QUIC traffic."
msgstr "当链路存在较高丢包或高延迟、传统 TCP 套 TCP 风格设计表现较差时，Hysteria 2 尤其有价值。但它并不是所有 TCP 协议的通用替代品：网络必须能够稳定承载 UDP/QUIC 流量。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md
msgid "Protocol Layers"
msgstr "协议分层"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/reality.md
msgid "A useful mental model is:"
msgstr "可以用下面的模型来理解："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The protocol depends on standard QUIC and the QUIC unreliable datagram extension. Authentication is performed through an HTTP/3 request before proxy requests are accepted."
msgstr "该协议依赖标准 QUIC 以及 QUIC 不可靠数据报扩展。在接受代理请求之前，会先通过 HTTP/3 请求完成认证。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Connection and Authentication Flow"
msgstr "连接与认证流程"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The client establishes a QUIC connection to the server."
msgstr "客户端与服务端建立 QUIC 连接。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC performs its TLS-based cryptographic handshake."
msgstr "QUIC 完成基于 TLS 的加密握手。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The client sends the Hysteria authentication request through HTTP/3."
msgstr "客户端通过 HTTP/3 发送 Hysteria 认证请求。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The server validates the supplied authentication value and communicates capabilities such as UDP support and receive-rate information."
msgstr "服务端验证提供的认证值，并返回 UDP 支持情况、接收速率信息等能力。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Only after successful authentication does the connection become an active Hysteria proxy session."
msgstr "只有认证成功后，该连接才会成为有效的 Hysteria 代理会话。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "TCP proxy requests use new bidirectional QUIC streams."
msgstr "TCP 代理请求使用新的双向 QUIC Stream。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "UDP packets use QUIC datagrams and Hysteria's UDP message framing."
msgstr "UDP 数据包使用 QUIC Datagram 和 Hysteria 自身的 UDP 消息封装。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The official protocol uses a dedicated success status for its authentication exchange. Implementers should follow the current upstream specification rather than hard-coding behavior from older Hysteria versions."
msgstr "官方协议在认证交换中使用专用成功状态。实现者应以当前上游规范为准，而不要把旧版 Hysteria 行为硬编码进实现。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "TCP Proxying"
msgstr "TCP 代理"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Each proxied TCP connection is mapped to a QUIC bidirectional stream. The client sends a Hysteria TCP request containing the destination address and optional padding. After the server accepts the request, the remainder of that QUIC stream carries the proxied TCP byte stream."
msgstr "每条被代理的 TCP 连接都会映射到一个 QUIC 双向 Stream。客户端发送包含目标地址和可选 padding 的 Hysteria TCP 请求；服务端接受后，该 QUIC Stream 的后续内容用于承载被代理的 TCP 字节流。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "This gives independent stream-level delivery inside one QUIC connection and avoids coupling every proxied TCP session to a separate TCP connection between client and server."
msgstr "这样可以在同一条 QUIC 连接内实现相互独立的流级传输，避免每个被代理 TCP 会话都必须对应客户端与服务端之间的一条独立 TCP 连接。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "UDP Proxying"
msgstr "UDP 代理"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "UDP relay uses QUIC's unreliable datagram capability. Hysteria adds metadata including a session identifier, packet identifier, destination, and fragment information."
msgstr "UDP 转发使用 QUIC 的不可靠 Datagram 能力。Hysteria 会额外加入会话 ID、数据包 ID、目标地址以及分片信息等元数据。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "When a UDP payload does not fit into the available QUIC datagram size, the protocol can fragment it. Reassembly requires all fragments of a packet; loss of one fragment means that datagram cannot be reconstructed."
msgstr "当 UDP payload 超过可用 QUIC Datagram 大小时，协议可以进行分片。重组要求同一个数据包的所有分片都到齐；只要丢失其中一个分片，该数据报就无法完整重建。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Operationally, this makes MTU and path quality especially important for large UDP packets."
msgstr "因此在实际运行中，MTU 和链路质量对于较大的 UDP 数据包尤为重要。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Congestion Control and Bandwidth Information"
msgstr "拥塞控制与带宽信息"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 allows peers to communicate receive-rate information during the authentication exchange. Depending on configuration and the values exchanged, the implementation can use explicit bandwidth information or rely on a normal congestion-control algorithm."
msgstr "Hysteria 2 允许双方在认证阶段交换接收速率信息。根据配置和交换值，实现可以使用显式带宽信息，也可以依赖常规拥塞控制算法。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Do not treat configured upload/download values as guaranteed throughput. They influence transport behavior; the real path is still limited by RTT, packet loss, server capacity, ISP shaping, and the congestion-control implementation."
msgstr "不要把配置的上传/下载数值理解为保证吞吐量。它们会影响传输行为，但真实链路仍受 RTT、丢包、服务端容量、ISP 限速以及拥塞控制实现限制。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "HTTP/3 Masquerading"
msgstr "HTTP/3 伪装"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "An unauthenticated Hysteria endpoint is expected to behave like an HTTP/3 service rather than immediately exposing a proxy-specific protocol response. Deployments can serve ordinary content or reverse-proxy to another site for non-Hysteria requests."
msgstr "未认证的 Hysteria 端点预期表现得像普通 HTTP/3 服务，而不是立即返回代理协议专用响应。对于非 Hysteria 请求，部署可以提供普通内容或反向代理到其他站点。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "This is an operational behavior, not a reason to neglect normal TLS and server hardening. A Hysteria server remains a public UDP service and should be patched, rate-limited where appropriate, and protected from credential leakage."
msgstr "这只是运行层面的行为，并不意味着可以忽视正常 TLS 和服务端安全加固。Hysteria 服务端依然是公开 UDP 服务，应及时更新补丁、按需要限速，并防止凭据泄漏。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Optional Obfuscation"
msgstr "可选混淆"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The upstream protocol defines optional packet-obfuscation mechanisms. These sit outside the normal QUIC appearance and are intended for networks that interfere with recognizable QUIC traffic."
msgstr "上游协议定义了可选的数据包混淆机制。这些机制位于正常 QUIC 外观之外，主要面向会干扰可识别 QUIC 流量的网络环境。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The best choice depends on the network environment. Do not enable obfuscation by default merely because it exists: it adds another compatibility requirement between client and server and can complicate diagnosis."
msgstr "最佳选择取决于网络环境。不要仅仅因为存在该功能就默认开启混淆：它会增加客户端与服务端之间的兼容要求，也会增加诊断难度。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Conceptual Client Configuration"
msgstr "概念性客户端配置"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "A Clash-family profile commonly expresses a Hysteria 2 node with fields similar to:"
msgstr "Clash 系配置通常会使用类似下面的字段描述 Hysteria 2 节点："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "hy2-example"
msgstr "hy2-example"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "hysteria2"
msgstr "hysteria2"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md
msgid "skip-cert-verify"
msgstr "skip-cert-verify"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "This is a compatibility-oriented example, not a promise that every field name is accepted by every Chimera core version. Use the schema of the selected core as the source of truth."
msgstr "这是面向兼容性的示例，并不承诺每个 Chimera 核心版本都接受所有字段名称。应以当前选中核心的配置 schema 作为权威来源。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Server Deployment Checklist"
msgstr "服务端部署检查清单"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "A Hysteria 2 server needs:"
msgstr "Hysteria 2 服务端需要："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "UDP reachability on the selected listening port,"
msgstr "所选监听端口具有 UDP 可达性；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "valid TLS identity/configuration expected by the client,"
msgstr "符合客户端预期的有效 TLS 身份/配置；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "an authentication policy,"
msgstr "认证策略；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "sufficient UDP socket buffers for the target workload,"
msgstr "能够满足目标负载的 UDP socket buffer；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "appropriate firewall rules,"
msgstr "适当的防火墙规则；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "and a decision about ordinary HTTP/3 fallback/masquerade behavior."
msgstr "以及对普通 HTTP/3 fallback/伪装行为的明确选择。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "If a cloud provider, home router, or enterprise firewall blocks UDP, changing Hysteria settings will not fix the underlying reachability problem."
msgstr "如果云服务商、家庭路由器或企业防火墙阻断 UDP，修改 Hysteria 参数无法解决底层可达性问题。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Native TCP and UDP proxying on top of QUIC."
msgstr "在 QUIC 之上原生提供 TCP 与 UDP 代理。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Independent QUIC streams reduce cross-stream interference compared with one monolithic reliable stream."
msgstr "相较于单一大型可靠字节流，独立 QUIC Stream 可以降低不同流之间的相互干扰。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC connection behavior can perform well on lossy or high-latency paths."
msgstr "QUIC 在高丢包或高延迟链路上可能具有较好表现。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "UDP relay maps naturally to QUIC datagrams."
msgstr "UDP 转发可以自然映射到 QUIC Datagram。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "HTTP/3-facing authentication/fallback behavior provides a normal service path for unauthenticated requests."
msgstr "面向 HTTP/3 的认证/fallback 行为可以为未认证请求提供普通服务路径。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Requires usable UDP connectivity from client to server."
msgstr "要求客户端到服务端之间具有可用的 UDP 连通性。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Networks may block, throttle, or degrade QUIC independently of TCP/HTTPS."
msgstr "网络可能独立于 TCP/HTTPS 对 QUIC 进行阻断、限速或降级。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "MTU problems can cause disproportionately confusing UDP failures."
msgstr "MTU 问题可能造成非常难以定位的 UDP 故障。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Aggressive bandwidth settings can create loss rather than improve throughput."
msgstr "过于激进的带宽设置可能增加丢包，而不是提高吞吐量。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Optional obfuscation adds configuration and interoperability complexity."
msgstr "可选混淆会增加配置与互操作复杂度。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Keep certificate verification enabled for normal deployments."
msgstr "正常部署应保持证书验证开启。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Use high-entropy authentication credentials and rotate them when clients are retired."
msgstr "使用高熵认证凭据，并在客户端停用后及时轮换。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Do not expose authentication values in URLs, screenshots, or debug logs."
msgstr "不要在 URL、截图或调试日志中暴露认证值。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Treat HTTP/3 fallback content as a real public service and patch it normally."
msgstr "应把 HTTP/3 fallback 内容当作真实公网服务正常维护和打补丁。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Rate limiting and abuse controls may be appropriate on publicly reachable servers."
msgstr "对于公网可访问服务端，可以按需要配置限速和滥用防护。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 is listed as a current client-core capability. Validate the exact accepted configuration schema and optional features against the current `Chimera_Client` branch before assuming full parity with Hysteria's reference implementation or Mihomo."
msgstr "Hysteria 2 当前被列为客户端核心已有能力。在假定与 Hysteria 参考实现或 Mihomo 完全一致之前，应根据当前 `Chimera_Client` 分支验证实际接受的配置 schema 和可选功能。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Chimera stores and generates profile/runtime configuration but does not itself implement Hysteria 2 transport logic."
msgstr "Chimera 负责保存和生成配置/运行时配置，本身并不实现 Hysteria 2 传输逻辑。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The current server capability map includes Hysteria 2 inbound work, and the server documentation lists a Hysteria example configuration. Treat that as a stronger signal than a purely planned feature, while still validating TCP, UDP, authentication, and optional transport behavior separately."
msgstr "当前服务端能力地图包含 Hysteria 2 入站实现，服务端文档也列出了 Hysteria 示例配置。这比单纯的计划功能更能说明已有实现，但仍应分别验证 TCP、UDP、认证和可选传输行为。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Cannot connect at all"
msgstr "完全无法连接"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Confirm the hostname resolves to the intended server."
msgstr "确认主机名解析到了预期服务器。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Verify UDP reachability to the configured port."
msgstr "确认配置端口的 UDP 可达性。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Check firewall/security-group rules on both ends."
msgstr "检查两端防火墙/安全组规则。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Verify TLS name/certificate expectations."
msgstr "确认 TLS 名称/证书符合预期。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Check the authentication value."
msgstr "检查认证值。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md
msgid "TCP works but UDP fails"
msgstr "TCP 正常但 UDP 失败"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Confirm the server advertises/supports UDP relay."
msgstr "确认服务端声明并支持 UDP 转发。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Test small UDP packets first."
msgstr "先测试较小的 UDP 数据包。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Check MTU and fragmentation behavior."
msgstr "检查 MTU 与分片行为。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Check NAT/firewall timeout behavior."
msgstr "检查 NAT/防火墙超时行为。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Disable optional obfuscation temporarily to reduce variables."
msgstr "临时关闭可选混淆以减少变量。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Poor throughput"
msgstr "吞吐量较差"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Measure packet loss and RTT before changing bandwidth values."
msgstr "修改带宽参数前先测量丢包率和 RTT。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Compare with a TCP-based protocol to determine whether the path is specifically hostile to UDP/QUIC."
msgstr "与基于 TCP 的协议对比，以判断链路是否专门对 UDP/QUIC 不友好。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Avoid over-reporting available bandwidth."
msgstr "避免把可用带宽配置得明显高于实际水平。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Check server CPU, socket-buffer limits, and uplink capacity."
msgstr "检查服务端 CPU、socket buffer 限制和上行容量。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Inspect whether a VPN, ISP, or enterprise firewall is rate-limiting QUIC."
msgstr "检查 VPN、ISP 或企业防火墙是否正在限制 QUIC。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 protocol specification: <https://v2.hysteria.network/docs/developers/Protocol/>"
msgstr "Hysteria 2 协议规范：<https://v2.hysteria.network/docs/developers/Protocol/>"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md src\protocols/tuic.md
msgid "QUIC, RFC 9000: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000>"
msgstr "QUIC，RFC 9000：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000>"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC Datagram, RFC 9221: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9221>"
msgstr "QUIC Datagram，RFC 9221：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9221>"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "HTTP/3, RFC 9114: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114>"
msgstr "HTTP/3，RFC 9114：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114>"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC substrate before Hysteria authentication"
msgstr "Hysteria 认证之前的 QUIC 底层"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "There are two different handshakes to keep separate when reading a trace or implementing a client. First, QUIC establishes a connection over UDP and carries a TLS 1.3 handshake in QUIC `CRYPTO` frames. The TLS/QUIC layer establishes the server identity, traffic keys, QUIC transport parameters, and HTTP/3 (`h3`) application protocol. Only after that protected transport exists does Hysteria perform its own `/auth` exchange inside HTTP/3."
msgstr "分析抓包或实现客户端时，必须把两次不同的握手区分开。首先，QUIC 在 UDP 之上建立连接，并通过 QUIC `CRYPTO` frame 承载 TLS 1.3 握手。TLS/QUIC 层负责建立服务端身份、流量密钥、QUIC 传输参数以及 HTTP/3（`h3`）应用协议。只有这条受保护的传输已经建立后，Hysteria 才会在 HTTP/3 内执行自己的 `/auth` 交换。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "For standards-conforming QUIC DATAGRAM support, each endpoint advertises the `max_datagram_frame_size` QUIC transport parameter (`0x20`) during the QUIC/TLS handshake. The value is directional: it describes the largest DATAGRAM frame the sender of the parameter is willing to receive. A value of zero, or absence of the parameter, means DATAGRAM reception is not available under RFC 9221. An endpoint must not send a DATAGRAM frame until its peer has advertised a non-zero limit, and sending a DATAGRAM larger than the advertised limit is a QUIC protocol violation."
msgstr "对于符合标准的 QUIC DATAGRAM 支持，通信双方会在 QUIC/TLS 握手期间声明 `max_datagram_frame_size` QUIC 传输参数（`0x20`）。这个值是单向的：它表示发送该参数的一方愿意接收的最大 DATAGRAM frame。按照 RFC 9221，值为 0 或完全没有该参数都表示不支持接收 DATAGRAM。在对端声明非零上限之前不得发送 DATAGRAM；发送超过对端声明上限的 DATAGRAM 属于 QUIC 协议违规。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "This produces a layered state boundary that SOCKS5 does not have:"
msgstr "这形成了 SOCKS5 中不存在的一组分层状态边界："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC can support 0-RTT on resumed connections, but replay safety is an application concern. A Hysteria implementation must not assume that an earlier QUIC session ticket removes the Hysteria authentication boundary or makes a side-effecting proxy request replay-safe. RFC 9221 permits DATAGRAM use in 0-RTT only when the remembered peer limit is valid for the resumed connection."
msgstr "QUIC 在恢复连接时可以支持 0-RTT，但重放安全仍属于应用层问题。Hysteria 实现不能假定之前获得的 QUIC session ticket 会消除 Hysteria 认证边界，也不能因此认为带副作用的代理请求天然具备重放安全性。RFC 9221 只有在记忆的对端 DATAGRAM 上限对恢复后的连接仍然有效时，才允许在 0-RTT 中使用 DATAGRAM。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The shortest QUIC-varint encoding of the TCPRequest identifier `0x401` (`1025`) is the two bytes `44 01`. Do not hard-code those two bytes as a magic prefix, however: RFC 9000 allows non-minimal encodings for variable-length integers other than QUIC frame-type fields. A correct Hysteria parser decodes a varint and compares its numeric value with `0x401`."
msgstr "TCPRequest 标识符 `0x401`（`1025`）按最短 QUIC varint 编码时是两个字节 `44 01`。但不能把这两个字节硬编码成魔数前缀：RFC 9000 允许除 QUIC frame type 字段之外的可变长度整数使用非最短编码。正确的 Hysteria 解析器应先解码 varint，再把它的数值与 `0x401` 比较。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Multiplexing, stream limits, and TCP backpressure"
msgstr "多路复用、Stream 上限与 TCP 背压"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Hysteria multiplexes independent proxied TCP connections as independent QUIC bidirectional streams inside one QUIC connection. Loss on one stream does not force bytes from another stream to wait for the missing stream offset, but all streams still share the connection's congestion controller and path capacity. This is transport multiplexing, not an application-level `MUX` command."
msgstr "Hysteria 会把彼此独立的被代理 TCP 连接映射为同一条 QUIC 连接内彼此独立的双向 Stream。某个 Stream 上出现丢包，不会迫使其他 Stream 的字节等待这个 Stream 缺失的 offset；但所有 Stream 仍然共享这条连接的拥塞控制器和链路容量。这属于传输层多路复用，而不是应用层的 `MUX` 命令。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Reliable stream bytes are governed by two layers of QUIC flow control:"
msgstr "可靠 Stream 字节受两层 QUIC 流控约束："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "connection-level credit (`MAX_DATA`) limits the total stream data in flight against the peer's advertised allowance;"
msgstr "连接级额度（`MAX_DATA`）限制所有 Stream 相对于对端声明额度可发送的数据总量；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "per-stream credit (`MAX_STREAM_DATA`) limits one individual proxy stream;"
msgstr "每 Stream 额度（`MAX_STREAM_DATA`）限制单个代理 Stream；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "the peer's bidirectional-stream limit controls how many new proxied TCP streams can be opened concurrently."
msgstr "对端声明的双向 Stream 数量上限控制能够并发新建多少个被代理 TCP Stream。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Consequently, a client that cannot immediately open a new proxy stream may be stream-limit blocked rather than rejected by the Hysteria server, and a stream whose writes stall may be flow-control or congestion blocked rather than a failed destination connection. These transport states are different from a `TCPResponse status=0x01` application-level failure."
msgstr "因此，客户端暂时无法立即新建代理 Stream 时，可能只是被 Stream 数量上限阻塞，而不是被 Hysteria 服务端拒绝；某个 Stream 写入停滞，也可能只是被流控或拥塞控制阻塞，并不等于目标连接已经失败。这些传输层状态与 `TCPResponse status=0x01` 的应用层失败不同。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC stream directions can finish independently. Closing or resetting one proxied TCP stream does not inherently close the parent QUIC connection or the other proxy streams. Implementations should preserve TCP half-close semantics where their socket abstraction supports them and should scope stream-local errors to the affected proxy stream whenever the underlying QUIC connection is still healthy."
msgstr "QUIC Stream 的两个方向可以独立结束。关闭或 reset 某个被代理 TCP Stream，并不会天然关闭其父 QUIC 连接或其他代理 Stream。只要 socket 抽象支持，实现就应保留 TCP half-close 语义；当底层 QUIC 连接仍然健康时，还应尽量把 Stream 局部错误限制在受影响的代理 Stream 内。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC DATAGRAM framing, sizing, and backpressure"
msgstr "QUIC DATAGRAM 封装、尺寸与背压"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "A Hysteria `UDPMessage` is the application payload carried inside one QUIC DATAGRAM frame. RFC 9221 defines two DATAGRAM frame types, `0x30` and `0x31`; the low bit only determines whether an explicit QUIC-level Length field is present. Neither QUIC frame type changes the Hysteria `UDPMessage` layout."
msgstr "一个 Hysteria `UDPMessage` 就是一条 QUIC DATAGRAM frame 中承载的应用层 payload。RFC 9221 定义了 `0x30` 与 `0x31` 两种 DATAGRAM frame type；最低位只决定是否存在显式的 QUIC 层 Length 字段。这两种 QUIC frame type 都不会改变 Hysteria `UDPMessage` 的布局。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The usable Hysteria payload size is therefore smaller than a naïve `max_datagram_frame_size` calculation suggests. The sender has to fit all of these into one QUIC packet:"
msgstr "因此，Hysteria 实际可用的 payload 大小会比直接按 `max_datagram_frame_size` 粗略计算得到的值更小。发送方必须把下面这些内容全部装进一个 QUIC packet："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The effective ceiling can be reduced further by QUIC's `max_udp_payload_size` and by the current path MTU. QUIC DATAGRAM frames themselves are never transport-fragmented or retransmitted. If one Hysteria UDP packet is too large, Hysteria's `Packet ID / Fragment ID / Fragment Count` layer performs the application-level fragmentation described above, or the packet is discarded."
msgstr "实际可用上限还可能进一步受到 QUIC `max_udp_payload_size` 和当前 path MTU 的限制。QUIC DATAGRAM frame 本身既不会由传输层分片，也不会在丢失后重传。如果一个 Hysteria UDP packet 过大，就由 Hysteria 的 `Packet ID / Fragment ID / Fragment Count` 层执行前文所述的应用层分片，否则只能丢弃该数据包。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "DATAGRAM delivery has deliberately different backpressure semantics from TCP proxy streams. RFC 9221 DATAGRAM frames:"
msgstr "DATAGRAM 的背压语义与 TCP 代理 Stream 有意设计得不同。RFC 9221 的 DATAGRAM frame："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "do **not** consume QUIC connection or per-stream flow-control credit;"
msgstr "**不会**消耗 QUIC 连接级或每 Stream 的流控额度；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "are still subject to the QUIC connection's congestion controller and pacing;"
msgstr "仍受 QUIC 连接拥塞控制器和 pacing 约束；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "are ack-eliciting, but their application payload is not retransmitted after loss;"
msgstr "会触发 ACK，但其应用层 payload 在丢失后不会重传；"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "may be dropped locally if the sender cannot transmit them in time, or by the receiver if it cannot allocate resources to process them."
msgstr "如果发送方无法及时发出，可能在本地直接丢弃；如果接收方无法分配处理资源，也可能由接收方丢弃。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "This explains an important diagnostic case: TCP proxy streams may remain healthy while UDP relay loses packets under pressure. SOCKS5 UDP has a similar unreliable application expectation, but it uses a separate UDP relay socket; Hysteria's UDP traffic competes with its reliable streams inside the same QUIC connection's congestion-control budget."
msgstr "这解释了一个很重要的诊断场景：TCP 代理 Stream 可能一直健康，而 UDP 转发在压力下已经开始丢包。SOCKS5 UDP 在应用语义上同样是不可靠传输，但它使用独立的 UDP relay socket；Hysteria 的 UDP 流量则会与可靠 Stream 在同一条 QUIC 连接的拥塞控制预算中竞争。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Because `Packet ID` is only 16 bits, long-lived high-rate sessions inevitably wrap the identifier space. Senders should avoid reusing an identifier while an older fragmented packet with the same identifier can still be reassembled, and receivers should key reassembly state with at least the logical session plus packet identity and expire incomplete entries promptly. `Fragment Count=0`, a fragment index outside the declared count, inconsistent counts for one in-flight packet, or lengths exceeding the received datagram are malformed inputs and should be rejected without unbounded allocation."
msgstr "由于 `Packet ID` 只有 16 位，长时间高吞吐会话必然会发生标识符回绕。只要旧的同 ID 分片包仍有可能被重组，发送方就应避免复用该 ID；接收方的重组状态至少应包含逻辑会话和数据包身份，并及时淘汰未完成条目。`Fragment Count=0`、分片索引超出声明范围、同一个在途数据包出现不一致的 count，或长度超过实际收到的 datagram，都是畸形输入，应在不进行无界内存分配的前提下拒绝。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC connection congestion control shared by streams and DATAGRAMs, plus receive-rate signaling"
msgstr "Stream 与 DATAGRAM 共享 QUIC 连接拥塞控制，并额外交换接收速率信号"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Reliable flow control"
msgstr "可靠数据流控"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "TCP receive windows on each SOCKS TCP connection"
msgstr "每条 SOCKS TCP 连接各自使用 TCP 接收窗口"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC connection + per-stream flow control (`MAX_DATA`, `MAX_STREAM_DATA`)"
msgstr "QUIC 连接级 + 每 Stream 流控（`MAX_DATA`、`MAX_STREAM_DATA`）"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "No multiplexing in RFC 1928; normally one CONNECT per control connection"
msgstr "RFC 1928 不定义多路复用；通常每条控制连接只承载一个 CONNECT"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Many TCP proxy streams and UDP DATAGRAMs share one QUIC connection"
msgstr "多个 TCP 代理 Stream 与 UDP DATAGRAM 共享一条 QUIC 连接"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Failure scope"
msgstr "故障作用域"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "SOCKS reply failure normally ends that requested relay; transport loss ends the TCP control connection"
msgstr "SOCKS 回复失败通常只终止该次请求的 relay；传输连接丢失则终止 TCP 控制连接"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "`TCPResponse` error is stream-local; QUIC connection errors affect every proxy stream/session on that connection"
msgstr "`TCPResponse` 错误只作用于当前 Stream；QUIC 连接错误会影响该连接上的所有代理 Stream/会话"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Optional packet obfuscation"
msgstr "可选数据包混淆"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Salamander, optionally wrapped by Gecko before QUIC reaches the wire"
msgstr "Salamander；在 QUIC 数据到达线缆之前还可以再由 Gecko 包装"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Boundary Conditions and Error Scope"
msgstr "边界条件与错误作用域"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "A robust implementation has to distinguish errors at three different layers:"
msgstr "健壮的实现必须区分三个不同层级的错误："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "**HTTP/3 authentication:** any status other than `233` means Hysteria authentication failed and the client disconnects. The server intentionally does not need to expose a Hysteria-specific authentication error body."
msgstr "**HTTP/3 认证：**任何不是 `233` 的状态都表示 Hysteria 认证失败，客户端应断开连接。服务端有意不需要暴露 Hysteria 专用的认证错误 body。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "**Proxy stream:** `TCPResponse status=0x01` means the requested destination failed; the server closes that QUIC stream, while unrelated streams can continue."
msgstr "**代理 Stream：**`TCPResponse status=0x01` 表示请求的目标连接失败；服务端关闭该 QUIC Stream，但无关 Stream 可以继续工作。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "**QUIC transport:** malformed QUIC frames, DATAGRAM use without negotiated support, or DATAGRAM frames beyond the advertised transport limit can be connection-level protocol errors and therefore tear down every Hysteria flow multiplexed on that QUIC connection."
msgstr "**QUIC 传输：**畸形 QUIC frame、未协商支持就使用 DATAGRAM，或 DATAGRAM 超过已声明的传输上限，都可能构成连接级协议错误，从而终止复用在该 QUIC 连接上的全部 Hysteria 数据流。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Length-prefixed fields must be validated before allocation or slicing. QUIC varints can represent values up to 62 bits, which is far larger than any reasonable address, diagnostic string, or padding field. The wire type alone is not a safe allocation bound. Servers should impose practical limits on address, padding, message, fragment-reassembly, concurrent-stream, and UDP-session state."
msgstr "带长度前缀的字段必须先校验，再进行内存分配或切片。QUIC varint 可以表示最高 62 位的值，远大于任何合理的地址、诊断字符串或 padding 字段。仅凭线格式类型本身不能形成安全的分配上限。服务端应对地址、padding、消息、分片重组、并发 Stream 以及 UDP 会话状态设置实际可执行的资源上限。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The base Hysteria specification deliberately leaves some malformed application-message handling to implementations. Defensive parsers should fail closed on truncated varints, truncated fixed-width fields, impossible fragment metadata, and address lengths larger than the remaining message instead of trying to recover by scanning for a later boundary."
msgstr "Hysteria 基础规范有意把一部分畸形应用消息的处理策略留给具体实现。防御性解析器遇到被截断的 varint、被截断的定长字段、不可能成立的分片元数据，或大于消息剩余长度的地址长度时，应直接失败并关闭当前处理路径，而不是通过扫描后续边界尝试恢复。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "With endpoint-side QUIC/TLS secrets and suitable tooling, the investigator can separate HTTP/3 authentication, individual stream IDs, and DATAGRAM traffic. A standards-oriented trace of the QUIC handshake can also expose transport parameters such as `max_datagram_frame_size` before 1-RTT application data is decoded. Even then, remember that QUIC packet boundaries are not TCPRequest message boundaries: STREAM frames can split or coalesce application bytes."
msgstr "如果能够获得端点侧 QUIC/TLS 密钥并使用合适工具，分析者可以区分 HTTP/3 认证、各个 Stream ID 与 DATAGRAM 流量。按照标准解析 QUIC 握手时，还可以在解码 1-RTT 应用数据之前看到 `max_datagram_frame_size` 等传输参数。即便如此也必须记住：QUIC packet 边界并不等于 TCPRequest 消息边界，STREAM frame 仍可能拆分或合并应用层字节。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "For TCP, a decrypted stream begins with the varint value `0x401`, then the length-prefixed destination and padding, followed by a `TCPResponse`, then raw proxied bytes. For UDP, the DATAGRAM Data begins with the 8-byte fixed Hysteria header (`Session ID`, `Packet ID`, `Fragment ID`, `Fragment Count`) before its address-length varint. Those are useful dissector anchors after decryption, not plaintext signatures visible to a normal on-path capture."
msgstr "对于 TCP，解密后的 Stream 首先出现 varint 值 `0x401`，随后是带长度前缀的目标地址和 padding，再之后是 `TCPResponse`，最后进入原始代理字节流。对于 UDP，DATAGRAM Data 会先出现 8 字节固定 Hysteria 头（`Session ID`、`Packet ID`、`Fragment ID`、`Fragment Count`），然后才是地址长度 varint。这些字段适合作为解密后的 dissector 锚点，但不是普通链路抓包可以直接看到的明文特征。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Obfuscation is an outer packet transform below QUIC. It does not replace QUIC TLS, Hysteria authentication, or proxy framing."
msgstr "混淆是位于 QUIC 下方的一层外部数据包变换。它不会替代 QUIC TLS、Hysteria 认证或代理封装。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Salamander"
msgstr "Salamander"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Salamander prepends an 8-byte random salt to every QUIC packet and XORs the QUIC packet bytes with a repeating 32-byte BLAKE2b-256-derived mask:"
msgstr "Salamander 会在每个 QUIC packet 前添加 8 字节随机 salt，并使用由 BLAKE2b-256 派生、以 32 字节周期重复的 mask 对 QUIC packet 字节执行 XOR："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The receiver derives the same mask from the configured pre-shared key and the received salt, reverses the XOR, and passes the recovered packet to QUIC. This is traffic obfuscation, not an independent authenticated-encryption layer; QUIC TLS remains responsible for confidentiality and integrity of Hysteria traffic."
msgstr "接收方根据配置的预共享密钥和收到的 salt 派生相同 mask，逆转 XOR，再把恢复出的数据包交给 QUIC。这属于流量混淆，而不是独立的认证加密层；Hysteria 流量的机密性与完整性仍由 QUIC TLS 负责。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Gecko"
msgstr "Gecko"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The current upstream specification also defines Gecko as a wrapper around Salamander. Gecko only changes the treatment of QUIC packets with the long-header bit set. Short-header packets go directly through Salamander. A long-header packet is split into between 2 and 8 chunks, and every chunk is wrapped before Salamander processing:"
msgstr "当前上游规范还定义了作为 Salamander 外层包装的 Gecko。Gecko 只改变 long-header 位被置位的 QUIC packet 的处理方式；short-header packet 直接进入 Salamander。一个 long-header packet 会被拆成 2 到 8 个 chunk，每个 chunk 都先由 Gecko 包装，再交给 Salamander 处理："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "`chunkIdx` must be smaller than `totalChunks`, and `totalChunks` is in the range 2 through 8. All chunks of one original QUIC packet carry the same `msgID` and count. The receiver first reverses Salamander, groups Gecko fragments by source address and message ID, validates consistent metadata, concatenates chunks in index order, and only then gives the reconstructed long-header packet to QUIC. Reassembly state needs per-source and global bounds plus a TTL to avoid turning handshake camouflage into an allocation attack surface."
msgstr "`chunkIdx` 必须小于 `totalChunks`，而 `totalChunks` 的取值范围是 2 到 8。同一个原始 QUIC packet 的所有 chunk 都携带相同的 `msgID` 和 count。接收方首先逆转 Salamander，然后按源地址和 message ID 对 Gecko 分片分组，校验元数据一致性，按索引顺序拼接 chunk，最后才把重建出的 long-header packet 交给 QUIC。重组状态必须具有按源地址的上限、全局上限以及 TTL，避免握手伪装机制本身变成内存分配攻击面。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The practical capture consequence is significant. Without obfuscation, QUIC long-header structure is visible even though its payload is encrypted. With Salamander, the UDP payload no longer parses as ordinary QUIC. With Gecko, one QUIC handshake packet can additionally appear as several independently padded UDP datagrams. Client and server must agree on the obfuscation mode and key before QUIC itself can establish a connection."
msgstr "这会显著改变抓包表现。未开启混淆时，即使 QUIC payload 已加密，long-header 结构仍然可见；开启 Salamander 后，UDP payload 将不再能按普通 QUIC 解析；再加上 Gecko 后，一个 QUIC 握手 packet 还可能表现为多个分别带随机 padding 的 UDP datagram。客户端与服务端必须在 QUIC 自身建立连接之前就对混淆模式和密钥达成一致。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Using TLS to Secure QUIC, RFC 9001: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001>"
msgstr "使用 TLS 保护 QUIC，RFC 9001：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001>"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC Loss Detection and Congestion Control, RFC 9002: <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002>"
msgstr "QUIC 丢包检测与拥塞控制，RFC 9002：<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002>"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Wire-Level State Machine"
msgstr "线级状态机"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Hysteria 2 has two control transitions before proxy payload is accepted. QUIC/TLS first establishes a protected connection; an HTTP/3 authentication exchange then changes that connection from an ordinary HTTP/3 service into a Hysteria proxy session."
msgstr "Hysteria 2 在接受代理负载前存在两次控制状态转换。首先由 QUIC/TLS 建立受保护连接；随后通过 HTTP/3 认证交换，将该连接从普通 HTTP/3 服务切换为 Hysteria 代理会话。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "A server MUST NOT interpret proxy requests before HTTP/3 authentication succeeds. A client must treat any authentication status other than `233` as failure and disconnect. This boundary matters when the endpoint also serves real HTTP/3 content or reverse-proxy masquerading."
msgstr "在 HTTP/3 认证成功之前，服务端绝不能解释代理请求。客户端必须把除 `233` 之外的任何认证状态都视为失败并断开连接。当同一端点同时提供真实 HTTP/3 内容或反向代理伪装时，这个边界尤其重要。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Authentication request and response"
msgstr "认证请求与响应"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "`Hysteria-CC-RX` is transport feedback, not authentication material. `0` means the client does not know its receive rate. Padding is ignored semantically."
msgstr "`Hysteria-CC-RX` 是传输反馈，而不是认证材料。`0` 表示客户端不知道自己的接收速率。Padding 在语义上会被忽略。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Success returns:"
msgstr "成功时返回："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Unlike SOCKS5, there is no separate one-byte method-selection exchange. Credential validation and transport capability negotiation are carried inside an HTTP/3 exchange protected by QUIC TLS. On authentication failure, the server deliberately behaves as an ordinary HTTP/3 service or forwards the request upstream instead of emitting a stable Hysteria-specific failure frame."
msgstr "与 SOCKS5 不同，Hysteria 2 没有单独的一字节认证方法选择交换。凭据校验与传输能力协商都承载在受 QUIC TLS 保护的 HTTP/3 交换中。认证失败时，服务端会有意表现得像普通 HTTP/3 服务，或把请求转发到上游，而不是发送一个稳定、可识别的 Hysteria 专用失败帧。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "TCPRequest and TCPResponse wire format"
msgstr "TCPRequest 与 TCPResponse 线格式"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "All multibyte fixed-width integers in Hysteria 2 are big-endian, while `varint` uses the QUIC variable-length integer encoding from RFC 9000."
msgstr "Hysteria 2 中所有固定宽度的多字节整数都使用大端序，而 `varint` 使用 RFC 9000 定义的 QUIC 可变长度整数编码。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Each proxied TCP connection starts on a newly opened QUIC bidirectional stream:"
msgstr "每个被代理的 TCP 连接都会从一个新建的 QUIC 双向流开始："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "```text\nTCPRequest\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n| varint 0x401         | message/type identifier          |\n| varint addr_len      | byte length of address string    |\n| addr_len bytes       | destination as \"host:port\"       |\n| varint padding_len   | random padding byte count        |\n| padding_len bytes    | random padding                    |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n```"
msgstr "```text\nTCPRequest\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n| varint 0x401         | 消息/类型标识                     |\n| varint addr_len      | 地址字符串字节长度                |\n| addr_len bytes       | 目标地址，形式为 \"host:port\"      |\n| varint padding_len   | 随机填充字节数量                  |\n| padding_len bytes    | 随机填充                          |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n```"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The address is a textual `host:port` string rather than SOCKS5's binary `ATYP | DST.ADDR | DST.PORT` tuple. A parser therefore has to honor the explicit byte length first and only then interpret the resulting string as an endpoint. Do not search the incoming stream for a colon or assume an IPv4-shaped address."
msgstr "地址是文本形式的 `host:port` 字符串，而不是 SOCKS5 的二进制 `ATYP | DST.ADDR | DST.PORT` 元组。因此解析器必须先严格读取显式字节长度，再把得到的字符串解释为端点。不能简单在输入流中搜索冒号，也不能假设地址一定长得像 IPv4。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The server answers on the same QUIC stream:"
msgstr "服务端在同一个 QUIC 流上响应："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "On `0x00`, everything after the response belongs to the proxied byte stream. On `0x01`, the server closes that QUIC stream. This transition is analogous to a successful SOCKS5 `CONNECT` reply followed by raw relay, but it occurs on one QUIC stream among potentially many concurrent proxy streams."
msgstr "当状态为 `0x00` 时，响应之后的所有内容都属于被代理的字节流；当状态为 `0x01` 时，服务端关闭该 QUIC 流。这个状态转换类似 SOCKS5 `CONNECT` 成功回复后进入原始字节转发，但它只发生在一个 QUIC 流上，而同一 QUIC 连接中还可能并发存在许多其他代理流。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "Stream parser boundary"
msgstr "流解析边界"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "QUIC provides an ordered byte stream, not message-sized reads. A single read can contain only part of a varint, exactly one request, or the request plus later bytes. Implementations should therefore parse incrementally and preserve any bytes already read beyond the control message. Treating one socket/stream read as one `TCPRequest` is incorrect for the same reason it is incorrect for a SOCKS5 request on TCP."
msgstr "QUIC 提供的是有序字节流，而不是按消息大小切分的读取结果。一次读取可能只得到 varint 的一部分、恰好一个请求，或请求再加上后续字节。因此实现必须增量解析，并保留已经超前读取到控制消息之后的字节。把一次 socket/stream 读取等同于一个 `TCPRequest` 是错误的，原因与在 TCP 上把一次读取等同于一个 SOCKS5 请求完全相同。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "UDPMessage wire format"
msgstr "UDPMessage 线格式"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "UDP does not open a QUIC stream. Each direction sends a complete Hysteria `UDPMessage` through QUIC DATAGRAM:"
msgstr "UDP 不会打开 QUIC 流。通信双方都通过 QUIC DATAGRAM 发送完整的 Hysteria `UDPMessage`："

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "```text\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n| uint32 session_id    | logical UDP association          |\n| uint16 packet_id     | packet identity for fragments    |\n| uint8 fragment_id    | zero-based fragment index        |\n| uint8 fragment_count | total fragments                  |\n| varint addr_len      | byte length of \"host:port\"       |\n| addr_len bytes       | destination/source endpoint      |\n| remaining bytes      | UDP payload fragment             |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n```"
msgstr "```text\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n| uint32 session_id    | 逻辑 UDP 关联                    |\n| uint16 packet_id     | 分片所属数据包标识                |\n| uint8 fragment_id    | 从 0 开始的分片索引               |\n| uint8 fragment_count | 分片总数                          |\n| varint addr_len      | \"host:port\" 的字节长度            |\n| addr_len bytes       | 目标/来源端点                     |\n| remaining bytes      | UDP 负载分片                      |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------+\n```"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "The client chooses a unique `Session ID` for each logical UDP session. The server normally associates a distinct outbound UDP source port with that ID so that replies can be mapped back to the correct client-side flow."
msgstr "客户端为每个逻辑 UDP 会话选择唯一的 `Session ID`。服务端通常会为该 ID 关联一个独立的出站 UDP 源端口，从而把返回的数据正确映射回客户端对应的数据流。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "There is no explicit `UDP CLOSE` command. The client may reuse a Session ID, and the server expires its mapping according to inactivity or implementation policy. If an expired ID later appears again, the server treats it as a new UDP session. This is a major lifecycle difference from SOCKS5, whose UDP association is explicitly anchored to the lifetime of a TCP control connection."
msgstr "协议没有显式的 `UDP CLOSE` 命令。客户端可以复用 Session ID，服务端则根据空闲时间或实现策略让映射过期。如果一个已经过期的 ID 之后再次出现，服务端会把它当作新的 UDP 会话。这与 SOCKS5 的生命周期模型差异很大：SOCKS5 的 UDP 关联明确锚定在 TCP 控制连接的生命周期上。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "If the server advertised no UDP support, received UDP messages should be silently discarded rather than producing a reliable error exchange."
msgstr "如果服务端声明不支持 UDP，那么收到的 UDP 消息应被静默丢弃，而不是再建立一套可靠错误交换。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "When one original UDP datagram is fragmented, all fragments carry the same `Packet ID`; `Fragment ID` runs from zero and `Fragment Count` states how many pieces must be reassembled. No fragment may be delivered upward until all pieces arrive. Loss of any one piece causes the entire original UDP datagram to be unrecoverable and it must be discarded."
msgstr "当一个原始 UDP 数据报被分片时，所有分片携带相同的 `Packet ID`；`Fragment ID` 从 0 开始递增，`Fragment Count` 表示需要重组的总分片数。在所有分片到齐前，任何分片都不能向上层交付。只要丢失其中任意一个分片，整个原始 UDP 数据报就无法恢复，必须被丢弃。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "For an unfragmented packet, `Fragment Count` is `1`; `Packet ID` and `Fragment ID` then have no semantic significance. Implementations should bound fragment reassembly memory and lifetime even though those resource limits are local policy rather than fields in the base wire format."
msgstr "对于未分片的数据包，`Fragment Count` 为 `1`；此时 `Packet ID` 与 `Fragment ID` 没有实际语义。即使重组内存与生命周期上限属于本地实现策略而非基础线格式字段，实现仍应对这些资源设置明确边界。"

#: src\protocols/hysteria2.md
msgid "SOCKS5 Comparison by Stage"
msgstr "按阶段与 SOCKS5 对比"

