msgstr "概念上的映射关系是："

#: src\protocols/socks5.md
msgid "Modern protocols generally did not replace the SOCKS5 idea; they expanded the control plane and moved more functionality into the protocol itself."
msgstr "现代协议通常并不是抛弃 SOCKS5 的基本思想，而是扩展控制面，并把更多能力下沉到协议本身。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "CONNECT on the Wire"
msgstr "线路上的 CONNECT"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP CONNECT is useful as the next comparison point after SOCKS5 because it solves nearly the same TCP-tunneling problem with a very different control encoding. SOCKS5 uses compact binary fields; HTTP/1.1 CONNECT uses an HTTP request and status response."
msgstr "HTTP CONNECT 很适合作为 SOCKS5 之后的第二个比较基准：它解决几乎相同的 TCP 隧道问题，但控制编码完全不同。SOCKS5 使用紧凑二进制字段，而 HTTP/1.1 CONNECT 使用 HTTP 请求和状态响应。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP/1.1 request"
msgstr "HTTP/1.1 请求"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "A minimal request is:"
msgstr "最小请求如下："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The request target is the destination authority: `host:port`. RFC 9110 requires an explicit port; CONNECT has no implicit default port. Unlike a SOCKS5 request, there is no `ATYP` byte. The host is represented textually and the HTTP parser separates the host and port according to CONNECT's authority-form semantics."
msgstr "请求目标是目标 authority：`host:port`。RFC 9110 要求显式提供端口，CONNECT 没有隐含默认端口。与 SOCKS5 不同，它没有 `ATYP` 字节；主机以文本表示，由 HTTP 解析器按照 CONNECT 的 authority-form 语义拆分主机与端口。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "At the byte level the HTTP/1.1 control phase is therefore variable length:"
msgstr "因此在字节层面，HTTP/1.1 控制阶段是变长的："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The empty line terminates the HTTP header section. Bytes after the successful CONNECT response are no longer ordinary HTTP/1.1 proxy-control messages; they belong to the tunneled protocol."
msgstr "空行用于结束 HTTP 头部。成功 CONNECT 响应之后的字节不再属于普通 HTTP/1.1 代理控制消息，而属于被隧道承载的协议。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Successful response and protocol switch"
msgstr "成功响应与协议切换"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "A proxy normally replies with a response such as:"
msgstr "代理通常返回类似以下响应："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "RFC 9110 defines **any 2xx response** to CONNECT as success. Immediately after the response header section, both sides switch to tunnel mode. A successful CONNECT response must not define a message body with `Content-Length` or `Transfer-Encoding`; clients ignore those fields if a non-conforming proxy sends them."
msgstr "RFC 9110 将 CONNECT 的**任意 2xx 响应**定义为成功。响应头结束后，双方立即切换到隧道模式。成功 CONNECT 响应不能通过 `Content-Length` 或 `Transfer-Encoding` 定义消息体；如果不合规代理发送这些字段，客户端应忽略。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "This creates a sharp state boundary:"
msgstr "这形成了一个非常明确的状态边界："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "For HTTPS, the first bytes after the 2xx response are normally a TLS `ClientHello` from the application. The proxy does not need to understand that TLS handshake when it is operating as a blind tunnel."
msgstr "对于 HTTPS，2xx 响应后的第一批字节通常是应用发送的 TLS `ClientHello`。代理作为盲隧道工作时，并不需要理解这次 TLS 握手。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Proxy authentication exchange"
msgstr "代理认证交互"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Proxy authentication is not a fixed pre-request negotiation like SOCKS5 method selection. An HTTP proxy can challenge a request with `407 Proxy Authentication Required` and at least one `Proxy-Authenticate` challenge. The client can then repeat CONNECT with `Proxy-Authorization` credentials."
msgstr "代理认证不像 SOCKS5 METHOD 选择那样是固定的请求前协商。HTTP 代理可以通过 `407 Proxy Authentication Required` 和至少一个 `Proxy-Authenticate` challenge 拒绝请求，客户端随后携带 `Proxy-Authorization` 凭据重新发送 CONNECT。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "```text\nClient -> Proxy\nCONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n\nProxy -> Client\nHTTP/1.1 407 Proxy Authentication Required\nProxy-Authenticate: Basic realm=\"proxy\"\n\nClient -> Proxy\nCONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\nProxy-Authorization: Basic <credentials>\n\nProxy -> Client\nHTTP/1.1 200 Connection Established\n\nClient <=============================> Destination\n              opaque tunnel bytes\n```"
msgstr "```text\n客户端 -> 代理\nCONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n\n代理 -> 客户端\nHTTP/1.1 407 Proxy Authentication Required\nProxy-Authenticate: Basic realm=\"proxy\"\n\n客户端 -> 代理\nCONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\nProxy-Authorization: Basic <credentials>\n\n代理 -> 客户端\nHTTP/1.1 200 Connection Established\n\n客户端 <=============================> 目标\n                 透明隧道字节\n```"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The exact credential bytes depend on the selected HTTP authentication scheme. Basic authentication, for example, is not encryption and should not be exposed on an untrusted clear-text proxy connection."
msgstr "具体凭据字节取决于选定的 HTTP 认证方案。例如 Basic Authentication 并不是加密，不应通过不可信的明文代理连接暴露。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 are framed differently"
msgstr "HTTP/2 与 HTTP/3 的分帧方式不同"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "CONNECT is an HTTP semantic, not an HTTP/1.1 text-format feature. With HTTP/2 or HTTP/3, the request is represented by protocol frames and pseudo-header fields rather than an ASCII request line. For HTTP/3, for example, `:method` is `CONNECT`, `:authority` carries the destination host and port, and the request stream remains open to carry tunnel data after a successful response."
msgstr "CONNECT 是 HTTP 语义，而不是 HTTP/1.1 文本格式专属特性。在 HTTP/2 或 HTTP/3 中，请求通过协议帧和伪首部表示，而不是 ASCII 请求行。例如 HTTP/3 中 `:method` 为 `CONNECT`，`:authority` 携带目标主机和端口；成功响应后，该 request stream 保持打开以承载隧道数据。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "This distinction matters in packet analysis: searching a capture for the ASCII word `CONNECT` works for clear-text HTTP/1.1, but not as a general detector for all HTTP versions."
msgstr "这个区别对抓包分析很重要：在明文 HTTP/1.1 中搜索 ASCII 字符串 `CONNECT` 有效，但它不能作为所有 HTTP 版本的通用检测方式。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Client and Proxy State Machines"
msgstr "客户端与代理状态机"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "A useful client-side model is:"
msgstr "客户端可用如下模型表示："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The proxy has a corresponding model:"
msgstr "代理端对应的模型是："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "A production implementation also needs limits for request-header size, parsing time, authentication retries, upstream-connect timeout, idle tunnel lifetime, and half-closed TCP connections."
msgstr "生产实现还需要限制请求头大小、解析耗时、认证重试次数、上游连接超时、空闲隧道生命周期，并正确处理 TCP half-close。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Capture-Level Walkthrough"
msgstr "抓包级流程"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "For an HTTPS request through a clear-text HTTP/1.1 proxy, a packet capture can look approximately like:"
msgstr "HTTPS 请求经过明文 HTTP/1.1 代理时，抓包大致会呈现为："

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "The final TLS arrows are logically end-to-end but their TCP bytes are relayed through the proxy. If the proxy performs TLS interception instead, that is a different architecture: two TLS sessions exist and the proxy is no longer a blind CONNECT tunnel for that traffic."
msgstr "最后的 TLS 交互在逻辑上是端到端的，但 TCP 字节由代理转发。如果代理执行 TLS interception，则属于另一种架构：此时存在两条 TLS 会话，代理也不再是该流量的盲 CONNECT 隧道。"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "SOCKS5 Comparison"
msgstr "与 SOCKS5 对比"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "HTTP CONNECT"
msgstr "HTTP CONNECT"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Proxy transport"
msgstr "代理传输"

#: src\protocols/http.md
msgid "Usually TCP; HTTP/2/3 can use their own mapped transport"
msgstr "通常为 TCP；HTTP/2/3 可使用各自映射的底层传输"

